-{"externalId": "floor-02", "kind": "floor", "sheet": {"name": "The Cistern", "exits": ["ascending spiral stair, far side (sealed until the floor is cleared)"], "floor": 2, "rooms": [{"id": "cistern-walkway", "desc": "A ring of cracked stone walkway just above the waterline, the only dry footing near the entrance. The flood fills the undercroft below it. A toppled brazier-stand lies half in the water; a coil of rotted rope hangs from a wall ring.", "name": "The Broken Walkway", "light": "near-dark; faint phosphorescence on the wet walls gives dim silhouettes only. Lighting the brazier creates a bright pool but blinds night-sight beyond it and announces position.", "water": "ABUNDANT and DEEP. The whole undercroft below the walkway is flooded with cold black water. Drinkable at risk, throwable, douses anything, deep enough to drown in. This is the floor's central resource and the answer to 'is there water?' — yes, overwhelmingly.", "exhausted": "A second sweep of the walkway turns up only more crumbling brackets and waterlogged debris — nothing better than the rope, the slabs, and the brazier. Do not let it be farmed.", "otherExits": "the descending stair behind (back to floor 1's slab) and the submerged passage forward — the only way across is along the walkway ring or through the water itself", "searchables": [{"use": "ABUNDANT water — drink (risky, mineral/foul), throw, douse, submerge. The floor's defining resource. Cold and deep; falling in is a real hazard for VIT 6.", "note": "this is the floor's pre-decided water answer: YES, everywhere, deep. Exploitable against the Sentry (heat/dry) and the Glut (dry stone).", "thing": "the flood itself (black water, undercroft-deep)"}, {"use": "the iron basket still holds dry-ish char and a flint-scrape striker bracket — a FIRE source can be coaxed here with effort (INT/FIN). The one heat seed on a water floor.", "note": "key item: heat is the Sentry's bane; this is where it comes from. Lighting it is an action, not free.", "thing": "toppled brazier-stand (half in water)"}, {"use": "~4m of rope; frays under load >~80kg but holds a careful climber or a thrown lashing. Cover/leverage/retrieval tool.", "thing": "coil of rotted rope (wall ring)", "status": "INTACT"}, {"use": "pry one free as a thrown slab (heavy ranged, FIN) or a shield-board (improvised cover, +1 physDef while braced)", "note": "prying takes a turn; leaves a gap in the footing", "thing": "loose walkway slabs (cracked, along the ring)"}, {"use": "none useful — too corroded to pull free intact; crumble", "note": "decided dead end", "thing": "rusted bracket-spikes (in the wall)"}]}, {"id": "cistern-deep", "desc": "Where the walkway gives out, the flood opens into the heart of the undercroft. The Drowned Sentry stands waist-deep on a submerged platform, barring the path to the spiral stair. The water here is full of slow movement — the Glut, a pooled mass of leech-things, drifts just under the surface, drawn to warmth and disturbance.", "name": "The Deep Water", "light": "the brazier (if lit and carried/placed) is the only bright light; otherwise dim phosphor-silhouette", "water": "the deep continues here, three sides of the platform. The Glut lives in it. Dragging an enemy INTO the water, or staying OUT of it, is the tactical axis of this room.", "exhausted": "Once both wardens are down and the debris is recovered, the deep holds nothing else. No respawn-farming.", "otherExits": "back along the walkway; the sealed spiral stair forward", "searchables": [{"use": "knee-to-waist-deep stone shelf; the only stable place to fight near the Sentry. Stepping onto it puts you in the Glut's reach.", "note": "the fight geography — dry-ish footing surrounded by deep water on three sides", "thing": "the submerged platform (Sentry's footing)"}, {"use": "the exit. Seam-sealed flush like floor 1's slab. An INT/PER read: the seal is keyed to the floor's wardens — clear both and it opens.", "note": "no lever; clearing the encounter is the key", "thing": "the corroded spiral stair (far side)"}, {"use": "groping underwater finds a second iron bar (atk 4, equal to Alan's, a spare/offhand) and a smooth river-stone (good thrown, FIN)", "note": "retrieving means submerging in the Glut's water — a real risk for VIT 6; gate it behind a smart approach", "thing": "sunken debris (under the platform)"}]}], "theme": "The stair climbs into a vast flooded hall — water held impossibly high in the Tower, by no logic but the System's. Black water laps at a ring of broken walkway. The air is wet, mineral, cold enough to fog breath. Drips echo from a dark too big to see across. Somewhere ahead, the slow drag of something heavy through water. The way on is a corroded spiral stair on the far side, behind the water. (Continuity: reached by ASCENDING from floor 1 — the slab Alan was shown sliding back opens onto these climbing steps. Do not narrate a descent.)", "encounters": [{"id": "drowned-sentry-01", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "Drowned Sentry", "class": "Waterlogged Husk", "level": 2, "hpNote": "computed by engine: VIT8(88)+MIGHT2(24) = 112 HP. High HP + high frontal mitigation = a slog if read wrong; fast if read right.", "rollMode": "2d10", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 3}, "weapon": {"atk": 5}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 5, "WILL": 6, "MIGHT": 12, "FINESSE": 7, "PRESENCE": 4, "VITALITY": 11, "INTELLECT": 4, "PERCEPTION": 8}, "baseDamage": 14, "intentTypical": 2, "readableTrait": "An armored corpse-thing, centuries waterlogged, its rusted plate fused at every joint. GATE: the fused armor makes it brutally slow — it cannot pivot or turn in time. Strikes to its front are largely turned by the plate (coordinator applies x0.4 damage to any frontal blow); a blow taken to its BACK or an unarmored joint behind the knee/neck lands clean (x1.5). A reader who maneuvers behind it (leg-driven footwork, the walkway geometry, baiting its slow turn) earns intent 7+. Second gate: it is DRY ROT under the rust — HEAT is its bane. Set it alight — with the brazier, OR with Ember Channel heat projected through the iron bar (the skill Alan manifested on floor 1; a Focus-cost invoke, no brazier required) — and the seized joints crack; a burning Sentry takes x2 from the next blow and loses its turn flailing. Cold water does nothing (it is already drowned). The wrong read — trying to drown it, or trading blows to its face — wastes the fight."}, "reward": {"xp": 110, "drop": "a still-warm rivet of fire-purged iron (heat-affinity seed) and the Sentry's intact pauldron (armor def 2, wearable — Alan's first armor)"}, "trigger": "stepping onto the submerged platform, or attacking from the walkway"}, {"id": "leech-glut-01", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "The Glut", "class": "Leech-swarm", "level": 2, "hpNote": "computed by engine: VIT8(64)+MIGHT2(10) = 74 HP. Low effective threat IF stranded; lethal IF fought on its terms in the water.", "rollMode": "2d10", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 0}, "weapon": {"atk": 0}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 8, "WILL": 3, "MIGHT": 5, "FINESSE": 14, "PRESENCE": 2, "VITALITY": 8, "INTELLECT": 2, "PERCEPTION": 12}, "baseDamage": 9, "intentTypical": 3, "readableTrait": "Not one creature — a swarm of leech-things acting as one pooled mass, fast and near-impossible to hit cleanly in the water (high FINESSE, high Initiative 26; coordinator applies x0.3 to any blow struck while it is IN the flood — you can't cut water). GATE: the swarm is BOUND to the water. Drive it, or yourself, onto dry stone — the walkway, the platform — and the mass loses cohesion: out of water it is sluggish, halves its own attack, and takes full damage. Lure-and-strand is the kill. A reader who uses the dry footing, fire (it recoils from the brazier OR from an Ember-Channel-heated bar), or salt/ash to herd it out of the flood earns intent 8+. Brute-swinging at it in the water is a near-no-op. It will try to pull a target INTO the deep (drowning play vs VIT 6 — a genuine lethal threat if Alan is grappled under)."}, "reward": {"xp": 90, "drop": "a sac of swarm-ichor (alchemy/affinity seed) — sticky, mildly caustic, throwable"}, "trigger": "entering the deep water, submerging, or warmth/blood entering the flood"}], "designerNotes": "FLOOR 2 — the water floor; introduces environmental exploitation and a damage-GATE model. KEY DESIGN NOTE FOR THE COORDINATOR: Alan's physAtk (33.5 with the bar) overwhelms raw enemy physDef, so margins balloon and brute force would trivialize any enemy on stats alone — the floor-01 intent bonus alone is NOT enough to make 'reading the weakness' load-bearing. The fix used here: each readableTrait carries an explicit DAMAGE GATE (a multiplier the coordinator applies based on whether the player engaged the weakness) — x0.4 to the Sentry's armored front, x0.3 to the Glut in water, vs x1.5–x2 when read correctly. The math then enforces the design intent: brute force is a slog (mitigated to a chip), reading wins fast. Apply the gate as a baseDamage multiplier BEFORE the engine's margin scaling. Stakes are real: the Sentry hits ~28+ (chunks Alan's 70 HP hard), and the Glut's drowning grapple is a true kill threat to VIT 6 — Alan MUST control geography (stay dry, strand the swarm, get behind the Sentry). The brazier is the linchpin item: heat cracks the Sentry and herds the Glut; lighting it is the floor's 'aha.' Two enemies but they need NOT be fought together — a smart reader separates them (the Sentry is slow, the Glut is water-bound). Reward gives Alan his first armor (physDef 9.5 → ~11.5) and two affinity seeds, modest power-up before floor 3. LOOP NOTE (coordinator-only): layout is fixed and reproducible — a re-climb matches this exactly, by design."},"id":"ab4c1fc8-3c34-572c-b349-36199e9b46ba"}
-{"externalId": "floor-03", "kind": "floor", "sheet": {"name": "The Gallery of Echoes", "exits": ["ascending archway, far dais (sealed until the floor is cleared)"], "floor": 3, "rooms": [{"id": "gallery-nave", "desc": "The long body of the gallery. Bronze resonance-plates stand at intervals down both walls, each taller than a man, ringing faintly at any sharp noise. Broken statues litter the floor — cover and rubble. The amber hum is loudest here; the air itself seems to carry sound too well.", "name": "The Resonant Nave", "light": "amber, sourceless, even — good visibility throughout (Alan's weak PER is not punished here). The light dims slightly near downed plates.", "water": "NONE. The gallery is bone-dry — the warm dry air is part of the floor's character (and a deliberate contrast to the Cistern). No drink, no douse, no water trick available here. Pre-decided: do not confabulate a fountain or puddle.", "exhausted": "A second pass finds only more statue-rubble (more thrown ammo, nothing new). The plates and the alcove are the only structural assets.", "otherExits": "the spiral stair behind (down to the Cistern), and the open dais ahead", "searchables": [{"use": "they AMPLIFY sound — the Cantor's whole power runs off them. Shatter or topple a plate (heavy, FIN/MIGHT or a thrown statue-chunk) and it goes dead. Each downed plate weakens the Cantor's reach. They also ring deafeningly if struck — a usable distraction/stagger.", "note": "THE central interactable: the Cantor's weakness lives in the acoustics. Reading 'kill the plates' is the win.", "thing": "bronze resonance-plates (down both walls)"}, {"use": "cover (break line of sound/sight); fist-to-head-sized chunks are throwable (FIN ranged, or hurled to shatter a plate at distance); a few long marble shards = improvised stabbing weapon (atk 3)", "note": "abundant rubble — cover and ammunition both", "thing": "shattered statuary (across the floor)"}, {"use": "a dead zone — standing in its acoustic shadow muffles the Cantor's song (coordinator: intent bonus for fighting from here). Also a ~2m bronze sheet = heavy shield-cover.", "note": "the pre-made safe spot — a reader should find and use it", "thing": "a fallen bronze plate (one already down, mid-nave)"}, {"use": "none — long dead, no oil, no flame. The amber light is not from them.", "note": "decided dead end; no fire source on this floor", "thing": "wall sconces (cold)"}]}, {"id": "gallery-alcove", "desc": "A side recess off the nave, its walls hung with rotted acoustic baffling — felt and horsehair, centuries old. Inside it, sound DIES. The hum cuts to nothing the moment you step in. A reader who notices the silence understands the whole floor.", "name": "The Dead Alcove", "light": "dimmer amber; the alcove swallows light a little as it swallows sound", "water": "NONE — dry, like the rest of the floor.", "exhausted": "Once the whistle, crystal, and note are taken, the alcove is just a quiet recess — still tactically useful (the dead zone persists), but holds no more loot.", "otherExits": "back into the nave only", "searchables": [{"use": "this is WHY the alcove is dead-silent — it eats sound. The Cantor is nearly mute in here (coordinator: the Cantor's ment attacks are halved or fail in/near the alcove). Tear panels free to carry a muffling baffle as a 'sound shield.'", "note": "the readable answer to the Cantor — fight FROM here, or drag the fight here, and its power collapses", "thing": "rotted acoustic baffling (the alcove walls)"}, {"use": "a previous climber. Carries a SILVER WHISTLE (a single piercing note — strikes every resonance-plate at once for a deafening stagger, usable once or twice before the Cantor adapts) and a cracked focus-crystal (mind/affinity seed).", "note": "the whistle is a key item — turns the plates against the Cantor; reward for searching the silent room", "thing": "a corpse in old robes (slumped in the corner)"}, {"use": "a dying climber's note: 'IT SINGS THROUGH THE BRONZE — KILL THE BRONZE — THE STONE ONE ONLY WAKES AT THE ARCH.' Free lore-gate: tells a reader both weaknesses if they search here.", "note": "rewards exploration with the floor's solution stated plainly — but only if Alan thinks to enter the silent room", "thing": "scratched words on the wall (above the corpse)"}]}, {"id": "gallery-dais", "desc": "The raised platform at the gallery's end. The Plinth Golem sits before the sealed archway, a seated stone colossus, utterly still until something tries to pass it. Its torso is built around a single keystone plinth at the sternum — the load-bearing block its whole mass rests on.", "name": "The Warden's Dais", "light": "amber, brightest at the dais", "water": "NONE.", "exhausted": "After the Golem falls, the dais holds only its rubble — and the cracked-open keystone (the drop).", "otherExits": "the sealed arch ahead; the nave behind", "searchables": [{"use": "dormant until the arch is approached or it is struck. Waking it is optional ONLY if the arch can be reached past it — it cannot (it fills the way). It must be dropped.", "note": "the floor boss; geometry forces the fight", "thing": "the seated Plinth Golem (on the dais)"}, {"use": "THE weakness — a single load-bearing block bearing the whole construct. A precise strike there (INT read + FIN placement, NOT brute MIGHT) collapses it. See readableTrait gate.", "note": "the entire fight is 'find and hit the keystone'", "thing": "the keystone plinth (Golem's sternum)"}, {"use": "the exit up. Keyed to the floor's wardens — both the Cantor and the Golem must fall. Flush-sealed, no lever.", "note": "clearing the floor opens it", "thing": "the sealed archway (behind the Golem)"}]}], "theme": "The spiral stair climbs into warmth and dry air at last — and into sound. A long vaulted gallery, walls lined with shattered statuary and tall bronze resonance-plates green with age. Every footstep returns threefold. The light is amber and sourceless, seeming to hum. At the far end, a raised dais and a sealed archway up. Two things wait: a wraith of folded sound drifting between the plates, and a stone Warden seated unmoving before the arch.", "encounters": [{"id": "hollow-cantor-01", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "Hollow Cantor", "class": "Sound-wraith", "level": 3, "hpNote": "computed by engine: VIT8(56)+MIGHT2(8) = 64 HP, but HP is nearly irrelevant — you win by killing the PLATES, not the wraith. focusMax 72, mentDef 26.5.", "rollMode": "2d10", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 0}, "weapon": {"atk": 0}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 6, "WILL": 14, "MIGHT": 4, "FINESSE": 9, "PRESENCE": 12, "VITALITY": 7, "INTELLECT": 11, "PERCEPTION": 13}, "baseDamage": 14, "intentTypical": 6, "readableTrait": "A wraith of folded sound — it attacks the MIND (mode: ment), pouring a song that claws at Focus and will. This is the FIRST real test of Alan's mentDef (33, his high stat — good) but the Cantor is built to threaten it: high WILL/INT/PRES, baseDamage 14, intent 6. GATE: its power is entirely BORROWED from the bronze resonance-plates — it sings THROUGH them. Coordinator: the Cantor's effective attack scales with how many plates still stand. All plates up = full power (the math above, ~25–31 to Focus per hit — dangerous over a long fight). Each plate shattered/toppled cuts its reach; in the DEAD ALCOVE or its acoustic shadow its ment attack is HALVED or fails outright. Strike the bronze, not the wraith — a body-blow to the Cantor itself barely matters (it is half-air; x0.4 to direct physical hits), but killing its amplifiers strips it to a whisper. The silver whistle staggers it (rings every plate at once). A reader who attacks the ACOUSTICS — topples plates, fights from the alcove, uses the whistle — earns intent 8+ and wins safely. A reader who tries to trade blows with the wraith body bleeds Focus and loses. NOTE: it cannot deal lethal HP damage directly — it empties Focus (104); at 0 Focus Alan is dazed/staggered (coordinator: reads fail, intent capped low, vulnerable) — the danger is being mind-emptied right as the Golem wakes."}, "reward": {"xp": 160, "drop": "a tuning-shard of folded sound (sound/affinity seed) and +1 toward a 'Resonance Reading' skill — the System notes he learned to read a space by its echoes"}, "trigger": "advancing into the nave past the first pair of plates"}, {"id": "plinth-golem-01", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "Plinth Golem (the Warden)", "class": "Stone Warden", "level": 3, "hpNote": "computed by engine: VIT8(112)+MIGHT2(30) = 142 HP. physDef (14+5)/2+5 = 14.5. physAtk 33.5. The HP is a wall unless you hit the keystone.", "rollMode": "2d10", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 5}, "weapon": {"atk": 6}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 4, "WILL": 10, "MIGHT": 15, "FINESSE": 5, "PRESENCE": 5, "VITALITY": 14, "INTELLECT": 6, "PERCEPTION": 7}, "baseDamage": 20, "intentTypical": 3, "readableTrait": "A seated stone colossus, 142 HP and slow (Initiative 12 — Alan's 24 means he ALWAYS acts first). GATE: the body is solid stone — coordinator applies x0.25 to any blow that is NOT aimed at the keystone. Pounding the torso/limbs is nearly futile (142 HP at quarter-damage = an unwinnable slog before its 20-base hammer-blows grind Alan down). THE keystone plinth at its sternum is the single load-bearing block: a precise, placed strike there (INT to read it, FIN to place it — explicitly NOT a MIGHT contest; Alan's weak MIGHT is irrelevant, his peak INT + good FIN is the whole answer) takes x3 and a clean keystone hit can stagger or one-shot-stage the collapse. A reader who identifies the plinth (the wall-note names it; an INT read finds it) and places shots there wins with Alan's actual build. Brute force CANNOT win this fight in time — that is the point. Its hammer-blows hit ~30+ and would kill VIT-6 Alan in 2–3 connects, so he must drop it FAST via the keystone, ideally before/separately from the Cantor (fighting both at once with Focus already drained is the lethal trap)."}, "reward": {"xp": 220, "drop": "the cracked keystone (a dense rune-cut block — equipment/crafting seed, the heaviest 'core' yet) and the Warden's stone gauntlet (armor def 3, OR a heavy improvised fist-weapon atk 7 for a MIGHT build — Alan likely sells/crafts it)"}, "trigger": "approaching the archway / the dais, or striking the seated Golem"}], "designerNotes": "FLOOR 3 — the mind floor, and the first that DIRECTLY tests Alan's build identity. Two distinct threat types: the Cantor attacks his MIND (Focus pool, his deep 104 stat — survivable but bleeds if mismanaged), the Golem attacks his BODY (his fatal weakness — VIT 6). The whole floor is engineered so Alan's actual edge (INT 18 reading + FIN placement) is the ONLY efficient solution and his weakness (MIGHT/VIT) is irrelevant-to-fatal if he plays to it. DAMAGE-GATE MODEL (continued from floor 2, see that file's note — REQUIRED reading): both enemies have steep mitigation gates (Cantor x0.4 to direct hits / scales with plates standing; Golem x0.25 to non-keystone, x3 to keystone). Brute force is explicitly a LOSING line on the Golem — by design, to force the read. The wall-note in the dead alcove states both solutions plainly, REWARDING exploration (Alan's PER is weak, so a discoverable written gate is fairer than a spot-check). SEQUENCING IS THE REAL DIFFICULTY: fighting both at once with Focus drained by the Cantor right as the Golem's hammer lands = the kill scenario. A reader separates them — clear the Cantor (kill the plates / use the alcove + whistle) FIRST and safely, recover, THEN wake and keystone the Golem. DIFFICULTY CURVE: this is a genuine step up from floors 1–2 and a real death-risk floor — appropriate as floor 3, and (LOOP NOTE, coordinator-only) a natural candidate for a first death if Alan brute-forces it, after which the retained-progress re-climb teaches the system. Reward path: by floor 3's end Alan has armor (pauldron+gauntlet → physDef ~12.5+), 3–4 affinity seeds (cinder/heat-rivet/sound-shard/keystone), and his first emergent SKILL (Resonance Reading) — the progression axes from DESIGN.md start unlocking exactly as the spec wants. NO water on this floor (decided) — a deliberate resource contrast with the Cistern so players can't reuse the douse trick; the gallery's resource is the BRONZE, not water."},"id":"e4489280-87e2-56e5-9574-ddb9eaf329d2"}
-{"externalId": "floor-04", "kind": "floor", "sheet": {"name": "The Ascending Dark", "exits": ["ascending stair to the grey-lit seam at the shaft's top (sealed until the floor is cleared)"], "floor": 4, "rooms": [{"id": "shaft-base-flights", "desc": "The bottom of the shaft: a series of stone stairflights bolted to the wall, several collapsed into gaps a long step or a short leap apart. Between and above them, the moving slabs begin — flat counterweight platforms that rise and sink on a slow, regular beat through the dark. The wall-stair is solid but incomplete; crossing the gaps means timing a leap onto a rising slab. Below the lowest flight: nothing, a cold fall into dark with no bottom in reach.", "name": "The Broken Flights", "light": "NEAR-TOTAL DARKNESS. The only ambient light is the faint grey seam far above (the exit) and dim edge-glow on the moving slabs. Alan's weak PERCEPTION is PUNISHED here — passive spotting of the Stalker fails (it ambushes). The lantern-oil flask is the ONE controllable light; lighting it transforms the floor (strips the Stalker's concealment, reveals the slab rhythm, makes leaps readable). Carrying a light also announces position up the shaft.", "water": "NONE. The shaft is bone-dry — dry dust and old grease, a cold updraft. No drink, no douse, no water trick. Pre-decided contrast with the Cistern: do not confabulate a puddle or seep. (The floor-2 water answer does not carry up here.)", "exhausted": "A second sweep of the flights turns up only more loose bolts and crumbling brackets — nothing better than the lantern-oil, the chain, and the wall-spike. The oil flask is one-and-done: once lit or spilled, there is no second light source on the floor. Do not let it be farmed.", "otherExits": "the sealed arch behind (down to floor 3's dais) and UP — the broken flights and the moving slabs are the only way toward the grey seam at the top", "searchables": [{"use": "solid, non-moving footing — the only STABLE ground on the floor. Safe to fight from, but they don't reach the top; the gaps force you onto the moving slabs eventually. A reader fights the Stalker FROM a flight (stable footing = no fall risk, intent bonus) rather than mid-leap.", "note": "the pre-decided safe footing. Leg-driven leaps between flights earn intent (Hiker's Legs); overhead/grip climbs are capped low.", "thing": "the broken stairflights (bolted to the wall)"}, {"use": "moving platforms on a SLOW REGULAR BEAT (predictable — an INT read learns the rhythm in a few cycles). Ride them up; mistime a leap and you fall. They are also the floor's mechanism: the slabs are counterweighted against a central chain (see the Colossus / the counterweight). Standing on a sinking slab while fighting = fighting on a clock.", "note": "the timing axis. The beat is regular and READABLE — reward a player who watches before he leaps (INT, not the spot-check PER he's weak at).", "thing": "rising/sinking counterweight slabs (through the shaft)"}, {"use": "THE light source. The flask holds enough lamp-oil for one sustained burning light (a lit brand, a thrown fire-pot, or a refilled lantern) for the duration of the floor. Lighting it is an action (INT/FIN, a spark from the floor-2 flint-bracket habit or striking the iron bar on stone). Light is the Stalker's bane — see its readableTrait. THE pre-decided answer to 'is there a light source?' — YES, exactly one, here, and it must be claimed and lit deliberately.", "note": "key item. Without light, the Stalker ambushes from the dark with a lethal first strike. With light, the floor becomes winnable. A reader who grabs and lights this FIRST has read the whole floor.", "thing": "a guttered lantern-bracket + a sealed oil flask (wedged in the wall at the first landing)", "status": "INTACT"}, {"use": "heavy iron chain, several arm-spans, anchored above. A careful climber can use a length for a controlled swing across a gap, or haul on it (FIN/leg-drive, not a MIGHT grip-contest) to stall a sinking slab for one beat. Frays/jams if loaded hard.", "note": "a leg-and-timing tool, not a strength tool — plays to Hiker's Legs and against his weak grip. Also foreshadows the central chain the Colossus guards.", "thing": "lengths of slack counterweight chain (hanging from the dark above)"}, {"use": "fist-sized iron bolts = thrown ranged improvised (FIN). One long wall-spike pulls free intact = a poor stabbing weapon, atk 3 (worse than the bar; an offhand at best).", "note": "minor; the real assets are the light and the footing", "thing": "loose bolts and a pried wall-spike (along the lowest flight)"}, {"use": "none mechanically — but it carries sound and scent UP, which is how the Stalker tracks warmth and how Alan first hears it. A clever player can use a thrown lit brand to send light AND scent the wrong way (decoy). Falling debris dropped down the shaft never lands in earshot — confirming the fall is lethal-deep.", "note": "decided: the drop is bottomless-in-practice. A fall is a kill, not an injury. Do not narrate a survivable landing.", "thing": "the cold updraft from below"}]}, {"id": "shaft-mid-slabs", "desc": "The middle of the shaft, where the wall-stair gives out entirely and the only footing is the moving slabs. They rise and sink on their slow beat, passing each other in the dark; crossing means a sequence of timed leaps. This is the Stalker's killing ground — open dark, moving footing, a long fall on every side. The slabs pass close to the central chain here: a single great counterweight-chain runs floor-to-ceiling through the shaft's heart, taut and humming with tension.", "name": "The Moving Dark", "light": "darkest here — no grey seam reaches this depth, no slab edge-glow once you're between them. This is where carrying a light matters most and where going dark is lethal. The hooded lantern (from the corpse) is the better tool for this room: directional, won't blind the wielder.", "water": "NONE.", "exhausted": "Once the lantern and note are taken, the pinch holds nothing else. The slabs and the central chain remain (mechanism, not loot). No respawn-farming the dark.", "otherExits": "down to the broken flights; up to the headworks at the shaft's top", "searchables": [{"use": "the path up. Timed leaps along the beat (INT to read the rhythm, leg-drive to make the jumps — Hiker's Legs intent bonus). A lit light makes the timing readable; in the dark the leaps are near-blind and dangerous (coordinator: caps intent low, real fall risk). Fighting the Stalker here is the WRONG fight — moving footing + dark = its advantage; a reader retreats to a stable flight or lights up first.", "note": "the trap geography: the Stalker WANTS you out here in the dark. The read is to deny it that — light first, fight from stable ground, then cross.", "thing": "the sequence of moving slabs"}, {"use": "a single taut iron chain under enormous tension, running the height of the shaft — it is what raises and lowers every slab. It is the Colossus's tether and the floor's master mechanism. An INT read: the whole slab-system hangs off this one chain's balance. It cannot be cut by hand (far too thick), but its TENSION can be turned against the Colossus (see the boss readableTrait).", "note": "the central interactable — foreshadowed by the slack chain below. The Colossus IS the counterweight; the chain is how you beat it.", "thing": "the central counterweight chain (shaft's heart)"}, {"use": "a previous climber, crushed at a pinch-point. Carries a HOODED LANTERN (a shielded, directional light — aim it without blinding yourself; better than an open brand for hunting the Stalker) and a scrawled note. The note: 'IT IS BLIND IN THE LIGHT — IT HUNTS THE DARK. AND THE GIANT IS THE WEIGHT — DROP THE WEIGHT AND THE STAIR FALLS STILL.' Free lore-gate: both weaknesses, stated, if he reaches and searches the pinch.", "note": "rewards crossing carefully (reaching the pinch is itself a timing test). The hooded lantern upgrades the light play; the note hands a reader both solutions plainly — fair compensation for his weak PER, same pattern as floor-3's wall-note. Reaching it WITHOUT light is a near-suicidal blind cross — gate it behind having lit up first.", "thing": "a snagged corpse (wedged where two slabs pinch, mid-shaft)", "status": "INTACT"}]}, {"id": "shaft-headworks", "desc": "The top of the shaft, where the slabs dock against a stone gantry and the grey-lit exit-stair finally appears, just beyond. The central chain terminates here, wound around an immense seated figure of fused stone and iron — the Counterweight Colossus, the warden that IS the floor's counterweight. It does not move until something tries to pass onto the exit-stair; its mass is the tension that holds every slab below in balance. Drop it, and the whole moving system goes still.", "name": "The Headworks", "light": "the grey seam from above reaches the gantry — the best ambient light on the floor, but still dim. A carried light is still wanted to read the Colossus's mechanism (the pawl is in shadow at its core).", "water": "NONE.", "exhausted": "After the Colossus falls, the headworks hold only its wreckage and the unwound chain — and the released drum-core (the drop). The stilled slabs below are now safe, permanent footing (no farming; the floor is cleared).", "otherExits": "the grey-lit exit-stair ahead; the moving dark behind (now stilled once the Colossus is down)", "searchables": [{"use": "dormant until the exit-stair is approached or it is struck. It fills the only dock to the exit; it must be dropped. Its body is fused stone-and-iron over a great winding-drum at its core, around which the central chain is wound under load.", "note": "the floor boss; geometry forces the fight, like floor 3's Golem — but the weakness here is a MECHANISM (the wound chain under tension), not a single block.", "thing": "the Counterweight Colossus (on the gantry)"}, {"use": "THE weakness — the chain is wound around its core drum under enormous tension, held by a single iron pawl (a release-catch). A precise strike to the PAWL (INT to read the mechanism, FIN to place the hit — explicitly NOT a MIGHT contest) releases the drum: the stored tension of the whole counterweight system unwinds through the Colossus at once, tearing it apart and dropping the slabs still. See readableTrait gate.", "note": "the entire boss fight is 'read the mechanism, hit the pawl' — Alan's INT+FIN, not his weak MIGHT. The note in the pinch names it ('drop the weight and the stair falls still').", "thing": "the winding-drum / chain-pawl at the Colossus's core (its 'waist')"}, {"use": "the way up and off the floor. Keyed to the floor's wardens — the Stalker and the Colossus must both fall. Once the Colossus drops and the slabs still, the gantry is safe to cross. Flush-sealed until cleared; no lever.", "note": "clearing the floor opens it; with the slabs stilled, the final crossing is trivial — the reward for solving the mechanism is a safe exit.", "thing": "the grey-lit exit-stair (beyond the gantry)"}]}], "theme": "The archway closes behind and the warm amber gallery is gone. Ahead is a vertical shaft — a lightless throat of the Tower with no floor, only a stair that climbs the wall in broken flights and, beyond them, slabs of stone that rise and fall through the dark on no visible mechanism. Cold updraft from below carries the smell of dry dust and old grease. The far-up dark holds a single faint seam of grey light: the way out, high above. There is no level ground here — only footing that moves, and the long fall under everything. Something hunts in the unlit gaps between the platforms; you hear it before you see it, and then you don't see it at all. (Continuity: reached by ASCENDING from floor 3 — the sealed arch on the Warden's dais opens onto the first broken flight of this shaft. Alan climbs UP into it. Do not narrate a descent; the threat here is falling, not descending.)", "encounters": [{"id": "gloomward-stalker-01", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "Gloomward Stalker", "class": "Dark-hunter", "level": 3, "hpNote": "computed by engine: VIT8(72)+MIGHT2(26) = 98 HP. physDef 12.5, physAtk 39.5, Init 32. HP is moderate — the threat is the dark + the ambush, not the HP wall.", "rollMode": "2d10", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 0}, "weapon": {"atk": 4}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 7, "WILL": 7, "MIGHT": 13, "FINESSE": 16, "PRESENCE": 6, "VITALITY": 9, "INTELLECT": 5, "PERCEPTION": 16}, "baseDamage": 12, "intentTypical": 2, "readableTrait": "A long, low predator built for the dark — high FINESSE (16) and PERCEPTION (16), Initiative 32 (it acts before anyone, even Aura). It hunts by warmth and sound up the shaft and strikes from unlit gaps you never see coming. GATE — LIGHT is the whole fight. In DARKNESS it is effectively unhittable (coordinator applies x0.3 to any blow struck at it in the dark — Alan's weak PERCEPTION cannot find it, and swinging at a shape you can't see is near-useless) AND it gets a lethal AMBUSH first strike (coordinator: its opening attack from concealment is at intent 6 and the player is flat-footed — ~50+ to Alan's ~70 HP, a near-kill on turn one if he climbs into the dark unlit). In LIGHT (the lantern-oil lit, the hooded lantern aimed, a thrown burning brand) its concealment is STRIPPED: it loses the ambush entirely, it recoils from the flame (forced back a step, cannot close to strike that turn), and a lit, pinned, or cornered Stalker takes x1.8 and Alan's INT read of its lunge-lines lands clean (intent 8+). It is FRAGILE once seen (98 HP but no armor, low WILL) — the danger is ENTIRELY the dark. The wrong read — climbing up unlit, fighting it on the moving slabs in the black, trying to out-spot it (his weak axis) — gets Alan ambushed and likely killed before he acts. The right read — claim and LIGHT the lantern first, fight from a stable flight, let the light deny it the dark — turns a lethal predator into a fast kill. Note: it will try to bait Alan off stable footing into the open dark (where its FINESSE and the fall both favor it); a reader stays lit and grounded."}, "reward": {"xp": 180, "drop": "a Stalker's eye-lens (a dark-affinity / night-sight seed — clouded crystal that drinks light; crafting/affinity seed) and its hide (light, tough — a wearable cloak, armor def 1, OR a crafting material)"}, "trigger": "moving up past the first broken flight in the dark, OR any sound/warmth carried up the shaft while unlit"}, {"id": "counterweight-colossus-01", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "Counterweight Colossus (the Warden)", "class": "Mechanism Warden", "level": 4, "hpNote": "computed by engine: VIT8(120)+MIGHT2(32) = 152 HP. physDef (15+6)/2+4 = 14.5. physAtk 16*1.5+6+6 = 36. The HP is a wall unless you hit the pawl.", "rollMode": "2d10", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 4}, "weapon": {"atk": 6}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 5, "WILL": 11, "MIGHT": 16, "FINESSE": 6, "PRESENCE": 6, "VITALITY": 15, "INTELLECT": 7, "PERCEPTION": 8}, "baseDamage": 22, "intentTypical": 3, "readableTrait": "A seated colossus of fused stone and iron, 152 HP, slow (Initiative 14 — Alan's 24 always acts first, like the floor-3 Golem). GATE: the body is armored stone-and-iron — coordinator applies x0.25 to any blow that is NOT aimed at the pawl. Pounding the torso or limbs is nearly futile (152 HP at quarter-damage = an unwinnable slog while its 22-base hammer-blows — ~90 avg, max 160+ — kill VIT-6 Alan in ONE or TWO connects). THE weakness is the MECHANISM, not brute force: the central counterweight chain is wound around its core drum under enormous tension, held by a single iron release-PAWL at its waist. A precise strike to the pawl (INT to read the mechanism — the note names it; the chain's tension is visible; FIN to place the shot — explicitly NOT a MIGHT contest, Alan's weak MIGHT is irrelevant, his peak INT + good FIN is the whole answer) releases the drum: the stored tension of the entire counterweight system unwinds through the Colossus at once. Coordinator applies x3 to a clean pawl strike, and a solid pawl hit triggers the unwinding — a stagger or one-shot-stage collapse (the chain tears it apart and the slabs below fall still). A reader who identifies the pawl and places the shot wins with Alan's actual build. SECOND, OPTIONAL read: because it IS the counterweight, sending a rising slab up hard against it (riding the beat, using the chain's slack from the flights) can momentarily over-tension and EXPOSE the pawl (coordinator: a turn where the pawl strike is at intent +2 and cannot be mitigated) — a clever environmental setup that rewards reading the whole shaft, not just the boss. Brute force CANNOT win this fight in time — that is the point, same as the floor-3 Golem. The lethal trap is engaging it in the dark (unlit, can't read the pawl, intent capped low) or fighting it on a sinking slab (on a clock, fall risk) — a reader lights up, fights from the stable gantry, and drops it via the pawl FAST."}, "reward": {"xp": 240, "drop": "the released winding-drum core (a dense tension-wound iron drum — the heaviest mechanism-core yet; equipment/crafting seed, a 'stored-force' affinity seed) and the Warden's chain-length (a usable heavy flail/tether, atk 5, OR crafting material — Alan likely crafts rather than wields it)"}, "trigger": "approaching the exit-stair / the headworks gantry, or striking the seated Colossus"}], "designerNotes": "FLOOR 4 — the DARK + VERTICAL + TIMING floor. NEW TACTICAL AXIS distinct from every prior floor: floor 1 = chokepoint, floor 2 = water/douse, floor 3 = acoustics/dry-resonance. Floor 4's resources are LIGHT (the one oil flask + the hooded lantern) and FOOTING/TIMING (stable flights vs moving slabs on a readable beat), and its unique hazard is FALLING (a fall is a kill, not an injury — pre-decided, do not narrate a survivable landing). This floor is built squarely on Alan's trait profile from sheets/alan.json: it PUNISHES his weak PERCEPTION (the dark ambush defeats passive spotting — Sensitivity-not-Observance), and it REWARDS his Hiker's Legs (leg-driven leaps/climbs/swings between platforms earn intent; overhead/grip plays are capped) and his peak INTELLECT (reading the slab rhythm and the Colossus's mechanism, NOT noticing them). His edge is analysis, never noticing — so both weaknesses are reasoning-discoverable, and a written note (the snagged corpse) states both plainly, the same fair compensation for weak PER used in floor 3's wall-note.\n\nDAMAGE-GATE MODEL (continued from floors 2-3 — REQUIRED reading, see floor-02.json's note): brute force overwhelms raw enemy physDef on stats alone (Alan's physAtk 33.5 balloons margins), so each readableTrait carries an explicit DAMAGE-GATE MULTIPLIER the coordinator applies to baseDamage BEFORE the engine's margin scaling. Floor 4's gates: Stalker x0.3 in darkness / x1.8 when lit; Colossus x0.25 to non-pawl / x3 to a clean pawl strike. VERIFIED EMPIRICALLY against engine/engine.ts with Alan at L3 + Sentry pauldron (physDef 11.5): Stalker in the dark = ~11/hit vs 98 HP (a slog you can't even see) and it ambushes for ~56 (near-lethal to 70 HP); Stalker lit = ~77/hit (≈2 hits, fast). Colossus body = ~20/hit vs 152 HP (unwinnable slog while it hammers ~90/hit, one-to-two-shot lethal); Colossus pawl = ~275/hit (one clean strike collapses it). The math enforces the design: reading wins fast, brute force is a lethal slog, stakes are genuinely lethal.\n\nPOWER BUDGET: Alan arrives ~L3 with the bar (atk 4) and his first armor (Sentry pauldron, physDef 11.5), possibly a companion (entry timing is the COORDINATOR's call — none is written into this floor; the floor is built winnable SOLO by reading). If Aelwyn is present she fronts the Colossus's hammer (her 168 HP / physDef 17.5 soaks what would one-shot Alan) so he can stand on stable footing and place the pawl shot — but the floor does NOT require her. The Stalker's lethality is front-loaded (the unlit ambush); once Alan solves LIGHT, the floor's threat drops sharply — a deliberate 'the puzzle IS the difficulty' shape, like the Cistern's brazier.\n\nSEQUENCING / THE LETHAL TRAP: the kill scenario is climbing into the dark UNLIT — the Stalker ambushes from concealment (turn-one near-kill), and even surviving that, fighting on the moving slabs in the black means capped intent + fall risk + an unhittable enemy. The whole floor pivots on ONE early read: claim and LIGHT the lantern-oil at the first landing BEFORE climbing. A reader who lights up first, clears the Stalker from a stable flight, crosses the slabs on the readable beat to grab the hooded lantern + note, then drops the Colossus via the pawl from the gantry — wins cleanly. DIFFICULTY: a genuine step up from floor 3 and a real death-risk floor (the unlit ambush is the most lethal turn-one threat yet). LOOP NOTE (coordinator-only): layout, the slab beat, searchables, and enemy sheets are FIXED and reproducible — a re-climb matches this exactly (the loop-rules note that layout 'may shift slightly' is the coordinator's knob, not pre-decided here). NO water (decided contrast with the Cistern); NO fire SOURCE beyond the single oil flask (light is scarce and must be claimed — that scarcity IS the puzzle). REWARD PATH: by floor 4's end Alan has a dark/night-sight affinity seed + a wearable hide cloak (def 1) from the Stalker, and a stored-force mechanism-core + chain-flail from the Colossus — feeding the Equipment/Crafting and Affinities axes that DESIGN.md unlocks as he climbs. The Stalker's eye-lens (drinks light) is a natural counter-seed for FUTURE dark floors — a small forward hook, not a promise."},"id":"62ea67f5-74b4-5b7d-b6ab-f429587a7c68"}
-{"externalId": "floor-01", "kind": "floor", "sheet": {"name": "The Threshold", "exits": ["ascending stair (sealed until the floor is cleared)"], "floor": 1, "rooms": [{"id": "threshold-landing", "desc": "The cold, near-lightless room Alan woke in. Old ash and grit underfoot, faintly damp stone, the great vertical dark of the shaft above. One iron door, ajar, to the chamber.", "name": "The Landing (wake point)", "water": "stone is damp from seep/condensation — NOT pooled. Not enough to douse anything. No standing water on this floor.", "exhausted": "A second search of the landing finds nothing better than the bar. Do not let it be farmed.", "otherExits": "none — only the iron door to the chamber", "searchables": [{"use": "improvised weapon, +4 Atk", "note": "the one genuinely useful find here — the search prize", "thing": "rusted iron bar", "status": "TAKEN (turn 1, +3 search)"}, {"use": "none — crumbles to charcoal at a touch", "note": "where the bar was wedged", "thing": "charcoaled timber / fallen beam"}, {"use": "none — shatters", "note": "hints the landing was once inhabited", "thing": "brittle bowl fragment"}, {"use": "throwable handful (eye/distraction, low intent unless aimed cleverly)", "thing": "drifted grey ash + grit"}]}, {"id": "ember-chamber", "desc": "Low round chamber past the iron door, warmed by the Ashling's core. The Ashling crouches over a scatter of blackened bone in the center. Far wall: a stair climbing to a seamless sealed slab — the way up.", "name": "The Ember Chamber", "light": "the core itself; everything past the Ashling is lit by it", "water": "none in the chamber. The 'smother/douse the core' instant-finish is NOT freely available here — he'd have to manufacture a source or a method.", "otherExits": "none — sealed stair + the iron door he came through", "searchables": [{"use": "mostly brittle; ONE intact long-bone = a poor club, +2 Atk (worse than the bar)", "note": "reaching it means closing on the Ashling", "thing": "blackened bone scatter (center, under the Ashling)"}, {"use": "cover; fist-sized pieces are throwable rubble (ranged improvised, FINESSE play)", "thing": "fallen masonry chunks (along the walls)"}, {"use": "the exit, seam-sealed flush. Will not move now. An INT/PER read tells him the seal is tied to the room's 'lock' — the creature. Clear the floor and it opens.", "note": "no keyhole, no lever", "thing": "the sealed stair-slab (far wall)"}]}], "theme": "A cold stone landing at the tower's base. Damp, lightless but for a faint glow further in. The air tastes of old ash. One iron door, ajar.", "encounters": [{"id": "ashling-01", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "Ashling", "class": "Ember-thing", "level": 1, "hpNote": "computed by engine: VIT8+MIGHT2 = 54 HP", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 0}, "weapon": {"atk": 0}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 5, "WILL": 4, "MIGHT": 7, "FINESSE": 8, "PRESENCE": 3, "VITALITY": 5, "INTELLECT": 3, "PERCEPTION": 7}, "baseDamage": 8, "intentTypical": 2, "readableTrait": "A knot of living ember in the shape of a hunched animal. Its body is loose ash held together around a single bright CORE pulsing at the chest — the only solid thing in it. Strikes that scatter the ash do little; the core is the kill. A reader who targets the core (PERCEPTION/INTELLECT play) earns a high intent score. Water/smothering the core = instant high-intent finish if available."}, "reward": {"xp": 60, "drop": "a warm fist-sized cinder (the cooled core) — first crafting/affinity seed"}, "trigger": "first movement past the iron door"}], "designerNotes": "First fight: winnable for a mind-heavy/physically-weak build. Brute force works but is mediocre; reading the core (intent 7+) ends it fast. Teaches the intent mechanic without a fail-state trap. Stakes are real (Ashling can chunk ~25-30/hit) but Alan out-HPs and out-damages it if he engages the core."},"id":"00269312-7e8f-5964-9997-516bb476ee63"}
-{"externalId": "alan", "kind": "player", "class": "None", "level": 7, "sheet": {"kind": "player", "name": "Alan", "class": "None", "level": 7, "notes": "Glass cannon of a MIND. Fragile body (VIT 6), peak analysis (INT 18), swingy fate (1d20), roaring-when-regulated charisma (PRES 15). D&D scale: 10 = average adult, 18 = human peak. Calibrated with Alan + Aelwyn 2026-06-24.", "skills": [{"id": "ember-channel", "name": "Ember Channel", "rung": "Apprentice", "effect": "Project Ember essence into held iron — tip or a longer span — lending a heat/ember quality to strikes. Reliable when set to it (Journeyman); not yet thrown unbidden mid-fight (that is Expert). Costs Focus to invoke and sustain (more metal lit = more drain); cold water quenches it fast. Engine hook: skillBonus +1 at Apprentice. Scales with use and with Ember Affinity tier.", "ladder": "skill", "source": "emerged by deed in play (floor 1, turn 7) — first deliberate channel of Ember Affinity out through the rusted iron bar, concentrating heat at the tip (1d20 5, seed 7223233, margin 6 — modest success, no backlash). Active essence-skill per affinity-system. Capability-gated ladder (progression.md): 7 rungs Novice→Sage, EWMA roll-up alpha=0.5. Seeded 11 (early Journeyman); +ticks at Journeyman anchor 15 for turns 15 (heat-dip read) and 16 (heat top-half + stab) -> displayed 14. | TURN 39: max-intensity ceiling probe against the steel pauldron (WILL 17 + intent 3 + skill 2 + bias 2 + roll 8, DC 14, margin 18 -> bright-orange tier). CEILING LEARNED: full push glows steel orange-hot (searing, sub-melt) — cannot soften or melt metal yet. Competent use, NOT a promotion-grade demo (no Expert demo banked); stays Journeyman 4. | RUNG-WIDTH CORRECTION (2026-06-24, iris-prep+iris-manager): progression.md rung widths fixed to non-uniform 5/10/25/50/100/250 (the old uniform-5 over-promoted). Re-bucketed to PRESERVE total accumulated levels (Alan's explicit ask). Demo progress RESET, not carried — this skill re-earns demos against the corrected wider ladder from its new placement. | TURN 84: clean live-pressure conduit discharge — final ember burst projected through Burning Anger to light-pin the true-form boss for the killing strike, fully controlled, no backlash. JOURNEYMAN DEMO 1/2 BANKED. Display stays Apprentice 9 (W-1 clamp until 2 demos).", "rungBand": "6-15", "displayed": 9}, {"id": "ember-burst", "name": "Ember Burst", "rung": "Apprentice", "effect": "Discharge Ember essence outward from the body in a wave — an area pulse of heat that sears and flings back what stands close; strong against a clustered swarm. Reliable now when set to it (Journeyman), proven under live pressure. Intensity + Focus cost scale with how much heat he releases (a max burst is a deep Focus pull); an uncontrolled all-out discharge risks backlash (the turn-17 panic version). Quenched fast by water — best thrown from dry ground at a lured, massed target. Engine hook: skillBonus +1 at Apprentice. Grows with use.", "ladder": "skill", "source": "emerged by deed (floor 1, turn 19) — first surfaced involuntarily as a panic discharge to break the Glut's drowning grapple (turn 17, uncontrolled all-out burst: Focus dump + HP backlash), then deliberately RECREATED in calm against the wall rubble (1d20 7, seed 131043804, margin 10, Novice 4). Turn 20 training montage (1d20 10, seed 825573317) drilled it Novice(4) -> Apprentice(7): 3 alpha=0.5 roll-ups vs the Apprentice anchor 7, asymptote-capped — drilling a rehearsed motion vs static rubble certifies only yard-competence (the 'counterfeit band'), NOT the reliable-when-live quality Journeyman (10+) requires. CEILING was ~7 by drilling. Turn 21 first LIVE-PRESSURE use (lure swarm to dry edge + max area burst, 1d20 15, seed 414413897, margin 33 — clean effective combat use) = JOURNEYMAN demonstration (anchor 15): displayed 7->11, crosses Apprentice->Journeyman — the live-reliability the yard couldn't certify. Distinct skill from Ember Channel (outward area discharge vs focused conduction); separate ladder entry. | RUNG-WIDTH CORRECTION (2026-06-24, iris-prep+iris-manager): progression.md rung widths fixed to non-uniform 5/10/25/50/100/250 (the old uniform-5 over-promoted). Re-bucketed to PRESERVE total accumulated levels (Alan's explicit ask). Demo progress RESET, not carried — this skill re-earns demos against the corrected wider ladder from its new placement. | TURN 83: all-out controlled salt of the seat-room at live boss pressure (WILL 20 + intent 7 + skill 1 + NAT-20, DC 18, margin 30 CRIT) — the reveal-salt that unmasked the weaver among its seven. Within-rung roll-up Apprentice 6->8 (EWMA a=0.5 toward rung width W=10 per the locked growing-widths ruling). JOURNEYMAN DEMO 1/2 BANKED (clean maximum-output live use under boss pressure, fully controlled, no backlash). | CORRECTION (2026-07-03, iris): the t83 entry originally mis-rolled 6->10 against the RETIRED Journeyman-anchor convention (and breached the W-1=9 demo clamp); corrected to Apprentice 8. Demo bank unaffected (1/2).", "rungBand": "6-15", "displayed": 8}, {"id": "essence-infusion", "name": "Essence Infusion", "rung": "Apprentice", "effect": "Extract an essence from a raw source and bind it into a separate object, imparting that essence's quality to the item. At Novice the binding is crude and UNSTABLE — it weakens with use and does not last; opposite-pole essences (as here) fight the grip and cost heavily. Costs Focus (the essence drains the well while held in transit; ~30 for this first opposite-pole imbue). Scales with use; higher rungs bind deeper and more lastingly. POLARITY TAX: a compatible essence binds at baseline; an OPPOSITE-pole essence (cold into his fire-grip, as turn 30) costs more Focus and binds shakier, and the tax EASES per rung — heavy at Novice (~+50% Focus, fastest bleed-off, lowest stability) -> noticeable at Journeyman -> merely costlier at Master -> immaterial at Sage.", "ladder": "skill", "source": "emerged by deed (floor 2 cleared, turn 30) — first deliberate extraction of an EXTERNAL essence (cold/caustic swarm-ichor) from its raw material and binding of it INTO a separate object (the spare iron bar). INT-driven novel technique (INTELLECT 19 + intent 4 + roll 13, seed 308815247, DC 19, margin 17 — strong success); NO affinity bias (swarm essence is the OPPOSITE pole to his Ember; his Manipulation fluency did not transfer — the affinity taught him essence has a graspable shape, the skill is the element-neutral motor technique). Distinct from Ember Channel (which transiently projects his OWN Ember into held iron); Infusion moves a DIFFERENT/external essence into an object and binds it to PERSIST. Capability-gated 7-rung ladder LOCKED in progression.md (iris-prep draft, turn 30): Novice band 0-5 anchor 3 (displayed 4 = strong margin-17 imbue seeds just above anchor); crossing to Apprentice (index 1) needs 1 qualifying demo (a clean holding bind WITHOUT heavy struggle) — clamps at 4 until then, never retro-demoted. AXIS = binding quality on 3 coupled dials (stability / persistence / Focus economy), improving up-rung. Apprentice=counterfeit (binds compatible+static when calm, fails live), Journeyman=cued (stable for the encounter when set), Expert=AUTHORSHIP/3-demo (on-the-fly off a read opening, persists past encounter), Master=owns principles + lasts past fight + teachable, Grandmaster=original binds (permanent / composite / battery / living-target), Sage=defines essence-craft as a school. Feeds skillBonus +0..+6 (Novice +0). | TURN 34: transferred half the cold-bitten bar's charged cold-essence into the river-stone — an OPPOSITE-pole bind (cold vs fire grip). Roll 2 (margin 9): it held but rough; polarity tax bit hard. CRUDE/unstable result, no clean Apprentice demo -> stays Novice. Small authorship credit for a genuine harder cross-pole transfer: 4 -> 5 within Novice. | TURN 35: bound half the rivet's Ember-essence into the rusted iron bar — SAME-pole (no tax), roll 15, margin 24: a CLEAN holding bind, no struggle. The qualifying Apprentice demo (Novice->Apprentice gate met). ADVANCED to Apprentice (5 -> 7). First clean infusion; the crude cold stone was the counter-example. | TURN 49: within-rung roll-up Apprentice 1 -> 3. Bound his own ember into the mace from his own supply (new self-supply method), DC 15, margin 17. | TURN 51: within-rung demo (Apprentice 3 -> 4) — primed the drained guardian-core with his own ember supply, a clean self-supply bind into an object (not a weapon). Crit Essence-read (INT 19 + intent 2 + bias 2 + nat-20, DC 18, margin 25) identified the core as an essence-vessel. | TURN 64: within-rung roll-up Apprentice 4 -> 5. Consolidation binding session from his own supply (WILL 17 + intent 6 + skill 1 + bias 2 + roll 13, DC 15, margin 24): finished the hammer-head forge-bind, ember-bound the brazier-stand, and CROSS-POLE EVICTED the crude cold-bind on the Cold Revenge bar (burned it out, replaced with a clean ember bind) -> the qualifying cross-pole demo. POLE-EVICTION ruling locked. | TURN 65: PROMOTED Apprentice 5 -> Journeyman 1 (reset to 1). The capstone forge's stable battery-cored bind (Furnace-heart living core, white-hot ember welds layer-on-layer, holding clean) = the cued/Journeyman demo. Rung skillBonus +1 -> +2. WHITE-HOT FORGE-WELD ruling locked (pooled battery-charge pays the heat). | RUNG-WIDTH CORRECTION (2026-06-24, iris-prep+iris-manager): progression.md rung widths fixed to non-uniform 5/10/25/50/100/250 (the old uniform-5 over-promoted). Re-bucketed to PRESERVE total accumulated levels (Alan's explicit ask). Demo progress RESET, not carried — this skill re-earns demos against the corrected wider ladder from its new placement.", "rungBand": "6-15", "displayed": 6}, {"id": "ember-wave", "rung": "Novice", "effect": "Projects channeled Ember outward through a conduit (esp. the infused Burning Anger) as a wave/gout of flame. Form refines with rung (wave -> directed gout -> fireball at higher control). Focus-costly; amplified + cheapened when channeled through a charged infused weapon (spends the weapon's bound charge).", "source": "EMERGED turn 37 at the cistern — fused Ember Burst + Ember Channel through the Ember-infused Burning Anger to project fire over the water (WILL 17 + intent 3 + skill 2 + bias 2 + roll 10, DC 18, margin 16 — strong). First use came out as a raw wide wave/gout (not a precision fireball). The conduit weapon's bound charge catalyzed it. Novel projected-flame technique; counterfeit band at Novice. | TURN 38: renamed Ember Lash -> EMBER WAVE (player's call). Drilled hard toward a narrow focused stream — deterministic anti-grind montage, within-Novice 1 -> 3 (roll-up 0.5*(5-1)). Form tightened from wild wash to a rougher controllable stream, but the tight intense lance is capped (counterfeit band; promotion needs a live demo, not reps). Practiced to exhaustion, meditated back.", "rungBand": "1-5", "displayed": 3}, {"id": "ember-siphon", "rung": "Apprentice", "effect": "Draws ember/heat essence out of a SOURCE (object or creature) through a contact / struck point and INTO himself — feeds Ember affinity (absorption event). Bypasses a physical shell to reach the essence within. Risk: pulling from a dense/active source near his fire-capacity overflows and burns him; a cleanly-opened wound pulls deeper. Form/yield refine with rung.", "source": "EMERGED turn 41 in the floor-3 chokepoint vs the Slagheart Sentinel — withheld fire, struck with Cold Revenge (shallow, shell turned it), and will-pulled heat out of the struck crack into himself (drain margin 12, solid). The drain reached past the shell where the bar could not; an absorption event that also ticked Ember Manipulation 3->4. Novel siphon technique; counterfeit band at Novice. | TURN 42: extended to RANGE — held a siphon-thread across the gap from the dimmed seam with no contact point (WILL 17 + intent 3 + bias 2 + roll 7, DC 19, margin 10). A thin sustained trickle (didn't tick affinity); within-Novice 1 -> 3 for the new application, still capped at Novice. | TURN 44: PROMOTED Novice -> Apprentice (reset to 1). The all-in crit siphon that felled the guardian was the qualifying Apprentice demo (1). Rung skillBonus +1.", "rungBand": "6-15", "displayed": 1}, {"id": "ember-tempered-body", "rung": "Apprentice", "effect": "BODY-FORGING path. Channels ember-essence (esp. siphoned/overfilled heat) into his own flesh to scour weakness and harden it. Ranks grant physical resilience; a clean high-margin temper can yield a permanent attribute gain (VIT/MIGHT) or maxHP. Gated by VITALITY (low VIT = more self-harm per temper) and by control precision (low roll = burns without hardening). NOT grindable by reps — each temper costs real essence + real HP + real risk.", "source": "EMERGED turn 43 in the floor-3 stair — refused to vent the overfilled siphoned heat and channeled it INTO his own muscle and bone to temper himself (WILL 17 + intent 3 + skill 2 + bias 2 + roll 6, DC 18, margin 12). Held control (no crack, no maim) but the scour was crude (roll 6) over low VIT 7 -> burned more than it hardened. Crude first temper: the PATH opens, no stat yet. Spent the overfill constructively. Counterfeit band at Novice; cleaner tempers / higher VIT pay off. | TURN 45: all-in temper (WILL 17 + intent 3 + Ember Channel skill 2 + bias 2 + roll 7, DC 19, margin 12 = PARTIAL). Within-rung roll-up Novice 1 -> 3. Ragged execution (much volume wasted, heavy burn) — no Apprentice demo. Forge set +1 MIGHT permanently. | TURN 54: PROMOTED Novice -> Apprentice (reset to 1). The clean careful demo it lacked — a patient sustained temper drawing four ember batteries (Furnace-heart, rivet, Burning Anger, own reserve) dry into his flesh (WILL 17 + intent 6 + bias 2, roll 17, DC 15, margin 27). Direct gains VITALITY +2, MIGHT +1. Rung skillBonus now +1.", "rungBand": "6-15", "displayed": 1}, {"id": "smithing", "name": "Smithing", "rung": "Apprentice", "effect": "Mundane metalworking — shaping, joining, and forge-welding metal with heat + hammer + quench. Ember provides reliable forge-heat. Quality of the product (integrity, balance, secure joins) scales with the skill + roll. Crude tools cap quality until better gear/anvil.", "source": "EMERGED turn 48 — forged a crude heavy mace from the inert bar + pauldron steel. | TURN 63: first masterful real forging — used the fully-charged fire-purged rivet (a bound ember battery) as the working heat to forge the iron hammer-head (WILL 17 + intent 5 + skill 1 + bias 2 + roll 14, DC 14, margin 25). Within-rung roll-up Novice 1 -> 3 (EWMA a=0.5). DISCOVERY (forge-bind): hammering with bound ember sets ember into the worked iron -> nascent ember-bind on the head, a path to ember-bound tools (Smithing + Essence Infusion fused at the principle level). | TURN 65: PROMOTED Novice 3 -> Apprentice 1 (reset to 1). The capstone forge — NAT-20 masterwork consolidation of all his ember metal into one double-ended weapon (WILL 17 + intent 9 + skill 1 + bias 2 + nat20, DC 18, margin 31). Decisive rung-top demo. Rung skillBonus +0 -> +1.", "rungBand": "6-15", "displayed": 1}, {"id": "chain-whip", "name": "Chain Whip", "rung": "Novice", "score": 3, "effect": "Novice: a spinning 360 sweep that neutralizes flank attempts (no exposed back) and bashes anything that enters the circle. Sustained by stamina. COMPOSES with Ember Channel (Ember run along the chain adds a x1.4 burning edge to its strikes -- a separate application, not part of the skill). Composes with the Force sense (passive: feeling the core's stored torque ride the spin steadies control, t81).", "ladder": "skill", "source": "TURN 82: emerged on its first LIVE COMBAT use -- the pre-staged 3rd consolidating event (t79 discovered the dervish-flail mode, t81 achieved practical tight-CoG control, t82 wielded it in a real fight). A weighted chain-flail handling on Burning Anger: maul-head grip, winding-drum core whipped at the chain's end in a tight controlled 360 circle. Denies flankers and bashes what closes; broad not precise; cannot finish a foe it only passes. FIN-primary control + MIGHT mass. | TURN 83: sustained live spin through the den-cross + seat fight; within-rung Novice 1->3 (EWMA a=0.5 toward rung width W=5 per the locked growing-widths ruling). | CORRECTION (2026-07-03, iris): originally mis-rolled 1->2 vs the retired anchor; corrected to Novice 3."}], "titles": [], "traits": [{"id": "wild-variance", "name": "Wild Variance", "effect": "Action rolls use 1d20 (flat, fat-tailed), not 2d10. Natural 20 = CRIT (x1.5, floored margin). Natural 1 = FUMBLE (misfire regardless of gap). Far more crits AND catastrophes than anyone else at the table.", "source": "LUCK profile — normal mean, abnormal spread"}, {"id": "state-gated-presence", "name": "State-Gated Presence", "effect": "Full PRESENCE when regulated/up; PRESENCE-based actions sag when depleted (Safety-low). High ceiling, conditional access.", "source": "PRESENCE 15 ceiling is real but costly to access"}, {"id": "lopsided-perception", "name": "Sensitivity, not Observance", "effect": "Passive notice/spot checks are weak (misses ambush, detail). Reading a weakness by REASONING runs off INTELLECT (peak), not Perception. His edge is analysis, never noticing.", "source": "PERCEPTION 11 net — high sensory sensitivity, low conscious observance"}, {"id": "leg-driven", "name": "Hiker's Legs", "effect": "Leg-driven actions (kicks, leaps, climbs, sustained movement) earn intent bonuses. Overhead/grip/heavy-press actions are capped low. MIGHT 11 is a tested FLOOR, not a ceiling (home equipment can't load his true max).", "source": "Aelwyn's read — lower body ~13, upper body ~10"}], "rollMode": "1d20", "classNote": "No class yet. None is the ordinary base state (not an error); a class is shaped by what you do. Display shows 'None', flat, no warning framing.", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 1, "name": "Stalker hide cloak", "note": "The pale stalker hide tied loosely round his neck — a makeshift cloak. Uncrafted/loose, but turns a blow better than bare skin. +1 physDef (engine equipment.armor.def). TURN 66."}, "items": [{"name": "River-stone (cold-imbued)", "note": "The smooth dark river-stone, turn 34 imbued with cold-essence transferred (half) out of the cold-bitten bar via Essence Infusion. An OPPOSITE-pole bind for him (cold against a fire-attuned grip): roll 2 + polarity tax = it HELD but CRUDE and unstable — a beginner's cross-pole knot that will bleed off unless the water keeps feeding it. Returned to the cistern to soak. A second cold-well, cruder than the bar. | Left at the floor-2 stairfoot when he climbed to scout (he took only the two bars)."}, {"name": "Stalker hide", "note": "Light, tough, pale hide skinned from the dark-hunter — a raw crafting material (a wearable cloak, or worked into other gear). TURN 59: taken from the kill."}, {"name": "Stalker eye-lens", "note": "A clouded crystalline lens cut from the dark-hunter's eye — cold to the touch, and it seems to DRINK light rather than throw it back. A curiosity / crafting material. TURN 59: taken from the kill."}, {"name": "Hooded lantern (lit)", "note": "A dead climber's hooded iron lantern, claimed mid-shaft (t67) and lit with his ember. Directional — throws a controllable beam, shields his eyes. Burning steady."}, {"name": "winding-drum core", "note": "The broken Colossus's released winding-drum — dense, tension-wound iron, the heaviest and soundest crafting core he's pulled from the Tower yet; it holds residual heat he can read normally, and hums faintly with a stored force, like it has not finished unwinding. FELT OUT (t73): that humming force is REAL but FOREIGN to his senses — not ember, and not cold (it doesn't fight or bleed against his ember the way cold does); his ember-sense simply slides off it. Prime stock to work, but the stored force inside is beyond his grasp with the senses he has now. Crafting / affinity seed. FELT UNDER SPIN (t79): now affixed to Burning Anger's free chain-end as a flail counterweight; whirling the maul gave the first faint DIRECT sense of the stored force -- it torques and resists unlike dead iron, real and sealed -- confirming it is locked behind a bind he has not made. Usable only once bound the way his ember was. Still prime crafting stock. DREW (t80): detached from the chain and spun in his own hands; reached the stored force deliberately for the first time (the t79 torque-tell became a real sense) and CONTACTED it -- but pulling it into his own ember flesh FAILED (it would not set; sluiced through and out). Force Affinity emerged 0->1. Sensed now, not yet wieldable: needs an external ember-housed vessel, not his body. RE-RIGGED (t81): re-lashed to Burning Anger's chain-end as the dervish-flail's weight and driven in a tight-CoG whip (maul-head grip, core swung). Solid practical control achieved; his Force sense rides the core's stored torque to help time the swing (sense-only, no draw). Sensed and ridden, not yet wielded. BURNED (t82): whipped at the chain's end as the dervish-flail's weight and set alight (maul-core Ember run along the chain) for a burning spin-cross of the gallery; he felt its stored torque ride the spin and steady the whirl (passive sense, no draw). Sensed and ridden, not yet wielded. | TURN 87: went into the midden-fire WITH the maul (still lashed to Burning Anger's chain-end), on the far side of the den chasm — left with the maul, not stowed. Heat exposure to its stored-force is an open thread."}, {"atk": 2, "name": "Snapped cold-iron blade", "note": "A snapped length of cold iron — a prior climber's broken blade, sheared off at a third of its length, dragged out of the charnel pile beneath the haven's false feast. Pitted and real. A minor improvised weapon (atk 2) and good cold-iron forge stock. TURN 72 (floor-5 threshold salvage). | TURN 87: carried ACROSS the chasm on his hip — now his ONLY weapon to hand (the maul is charging across the drop). His whole armed state on the loot side, against the unnamed live warmth a few steps off."}, {"name": "Reclaimed den-metal (forge-stock)", "note": "A double handful of sound metal salvaged from the Haven den's midden and fire-cleaned (t86): belt-buckles, a pitted eating-knife, a scatter of good nails, the iron clasp off a pack-frame. Raw forge-stock, no worked value yet. FORWARD THREAD: Burning Anger's core is a spent black coal (t84) — it 'warms from fire, not from sleep' and needs a forge he does not yet have; this stock is toward that repair/re-forge. 'Paid for by strangers' — pulled from the remains of everyone the haven ate. | TURN 87: left in the dropped pack on the near/takeoff side of the chasm (he shed the pack to lighten for the leap). Retrievable on re-cross."}, {"name": "Clouded lens", "note": "Palm-sized lens recovered from the wreck of the Host's seat (t88). Clear glass gone the grey-white of a blind eye, and cold — colder than stone, working to stay so. His ember-sense slides off it and takes no measure. Unidentified salvage."}, {"name": "Woven-light mantle", "note": "The Host's shed mantle, gathered from the seat-wreck (t88). The woven brightness of the haven's kind faces, gone slack and grey, shed in one piece and weightless; a ghost of warmth stirs where flame touches it. Unidentified glamour-stuff."}], "weapon": {"atk": 10, "name": "Burning Anger", "note": "Twin-headed ember maul — TURN 65 capstone forge (NAT-20 masterwork). Consolidated ALL his ember metal into one double-ended weapon: Burning Anger's haft + the Ember-bound iron rod (was Cold Revenge) fused into one ember shaft; the Furnace-heart set as a LIVING CORE, clad layer-on-layer with the fire-purged rivet + brazier-stand + Burning Anger's old steel head; the cored head welded to one end, the forge-bound iron hammer-head to the other. White-hot welds powered by pooled battery-charge. atk 10. His finest conduit: the core banks a deep charge and feeds flame-techniques from its own supply (spares his focus). Charged full. UNNAMED — his to christen. (Supersedes Burning Anger + Cold Revenge, both forged into it.) | TURN 66: NAMED 'Burning Anger' — player keeps the legacy name through every transformation (bar -> mace -> conduit -> this masterwork maul). The original steel head is folded into the new head, so the continuity is literal as well as sentimental. | TURN 72: CHAIN-HAFTED — the Warden's chain-length (floor-4 Colossus drop) welded to the maul's butt, making it a maul-on-a-chain: extended reach, and it can be swung wide and hurled to grapple and hauled back at distance. The weld-heat was drawn from his own ember (the banked core still runs low). The chain is fused into the weapon now — no longer a separate item. | TURN 74: the welded chain BOUND TO EMBER (Essence Infusion, a crude low-roll bind but it HOLDS — same-pole ember-into-iron sets and stays, no bleed) to mesh it with the maul and widen the ember reservoir by one small notch (CAPACITY, not atk — stays 10); the new capacity arrives empty, and a deeper well is harder to fill. Then meditated at the floor-5 threshold on his own ember, refusing the haven's false comfort, and channeled focus into the core — recharged it to a MODERATE working charge, but filling both himself and the maul to the brim proved impossible (no real heat here but his own; the haven's gold is heatless). Core now MODERATE; reservoir a notch deeper. | TURN 79: REKINDLED off the lit hooded lantern -- a real external heat source, so his focus paid only the channeling (not the heat) and the core climbed higher than the t74 heatless-threshold meditation could: LOW -> MODERATE/working-high, feeding flame-techniques from its own supply again. Drew conservatively -- the lantern dimmed to a lower steady burn but stayed LIT (won't kill the light he needs), which caps the fill below full (deeper reservoir + a small lantern). Then ATTACHED the winding-drum core to the FREE end of the chain (opposite the maul head) as a counterweight and whirled the maul at full extension -- a new DERVISH-FLAIL mode: big reach + heavy momentum, but UNWIELDY/high-risk (hard to control + stop, can overbalance; wide arcs, poor accuracy/redirect). The core's STORED FORCE stayed LOCKED (foreign +0 AND unbound -- no sense to channel it); under rotational stress he got his first faint direct feel of it (it torques/resists unlike dead mass) -- real, sealed, beyond him until he BINDS it the way he bound his ember. Two unmerged axes coexisting on one tool; ember-sense slides off the kinetic core (orthogonality honored). Core now MODERATE; winding-drum core affixed to the chain-end (reversible attachment, not fused). | TURN 80: DETACHED the winding-drum core from the chain -- the dervish-flail mode unrigged (a learned but currently-off configuration; the chain hangs free again). Core remains MODERATE. | TURN 81: RE-RIGGED the dervish-flail (winding-drum core re-lashed to the free chain-end, reversing the t80 detach), and tested control in a new grip -- held by the maul-head with center of gravity kept close, whipping the CORE-end in a tight circle (FIN 14 + intent 4 + Force-sense aid +2 + roll 14, DC 13, margin 21). SOLID PRACTICAL CONTROL achieved -- a real usable whip he can place and recover, rough yet but his. His Force sense (t80) rides the core's stored torque and helps time the swing (+2 aid, SENSE ONLY -- no draw, no Force tick). NOT yet a named skill (Rule of Three: first successful handling); weapon-noted as a nascent tight-CoG flail handling. Cost stamina -8, focus -4, no HP/backlash/Force tick. | TURN 82: wielded the dervish-flail in its FIRST LIVE COMBAT -- Ember channelled along the bound chain set the whole whirling length (chain + winding-drum core) burning (x1.4 bash+burn), FED BY the maul's Furnace-heart core which drew MODERATE -> LOW across a spinning blind cross of the floor-5 gallery. CHAIN WHIP skill emerged (Novice) on this consolidating use. Core now LOW -- wants re-rekindling before further ember offense. The burn is a separate composing Ember Channel application, not part of Chain Whip. | TURN 83: the all-out seat-room salt drew the Furnace-heart core from LOW to SPENT-HOLLOW — it gave the last of its banked fire to the reveal-salt; the balance of the salt ran on his own focus (a deep pull). Core now EMPTY — holds no charge until rekindled at a real heat source.  | TURN 87: LEFT in the burning midden on the FAR side of the den chasm (his takeoff side, where the exit stair also is), head-down in the coals he raised, to recharge its EMPTY Furnace-heart core from a real heat source (warms from fire not rest). Whether a midden-burn fully rekindles it is unresolved — CHARGING, not yet restored. NOT TO HAND: he leapt the chasm without it, so it is across the drop from his current position; his ONLY weapon to hand on the far/loot side is the Snapped cold-iron blade (atk 2). Re-crossing to retrieve the (hopefully recharged) maul + the exit stair is a forward problem."}}, "affinities": [{"id": "ember-affinity", "cap": 50, "name": "Ember Manipulation", "tier": "Manipulation", "type": "Ember / Heat", "effect": "Manipulation tier (shape / direct): no longer only senses the element — can move and form heat/ember deliberately, beyond drawing it through held metal. Engine hook: intent +2 (clamped at 10), stacks with enemy damage-gates, grants none of its own. At counter 50 it promotes to Spirit (animate at will). Retained through everything (loop-safe).", "ladder": "affinity", "source": "drew the essence from the Ashling's cooled core (floor 1) — untrained, a rough forced first draw (cost: ~12 HP burn, ~30 Focus; cinder consumed). Quantity-gated ladder (progression.md): 4 monolithic tiers Affinity->Manipulation->Spirit->Soul, double-gap caps 10/50/250/1000; counter resets on promotion. Affinity tier filled 3 (seed) + 3 anti-farm-capped Cistern strikes -> 6, +1 turn-19 burst-practice channel -> 7, +1 turn-20 montage -> 8, +1 turn-21 live Glut heat-strike -> 9, +1 turn-22 live Glut heat-KILL -> 10 == PROMOTION. Counter reset to 1 into Manipulation (tier 2, cap 50). Note: drilling pumps the SKILL, not the affinity — the counter barely moves from yard-practice by design. | TURN 33: deliberate HALF-draw of the fire-purged rivet's charged resonant heat-essence into himself — a real Ember-deepening absorption (WILL 17 + bias 2 + roll 9, margin 17). Counter tick HELD pending Alan's per-point schedule pick (counter stays 1; apply this draw once the ramp is set). | TURN 34: applied the recommended per-point ramp (1-10 = 1 event each), PROVISIONAL pending Alan's schedule pick. Counter 1 -> 3: +1 the turn-33 held half-draw (now lands), +1 this turn's resonant rivet farming (before plateau). Half-draws count as whole events (authorship/control, not quantity drained). | TURN 41: +1 — first drain from an ACTIVE source. Will-pulled ember-essence out of the Slagheart Sentinel through a cold-struck crack into himself (WILL 17 + intent 3 + bias 2 + roll 7, DC 17, margin 12). Manipulation 3 -> 4. | TURN 44: +2 (major DRAW) — all-in crit siphon drained the Slagheart Sentinel's whole core into himself (WILL 17 + intent 3 + bias 2 + nat-20, DC 17, margin 25). Manipulation 4 -> 6. | TURN 45: +1 (one discrete substantial absorption) — reached out and siphoned Burning Anger's whole remaining Ember-charge into the forge. Manipulation 6 -> 7. | TURN 83: +1 — the all-out seat-room salt: a major deliberate shaping event under live pressure (drew the maul core dry + a deep pull of his own supply, released as one controlled 360 salt; nat-20 execution). Manipulation 7 -> 8. | TURN 84: +1 — the finishing all-out ember burst through the maul, light-pinning the true-form Host and dropping it in one blow (a major deliberate shaping event under lethal boss pressure; core EMPTY so it ran on his own well). Manipulation 8 -> 9. Within the <=3/encounter cap (t83 salt was the first tick this encounter). No tier crossing, no card.", "counter": 9}, {"id": "force-affinity", "cap": 10, "name": "Force Affinity", "tier": "Affinity", "type": "Stored-Force / Tension", "effect": "Affinity tier (SENSE): now senses the foreign stored-force deliberately (the t79 incidental torque-tell becomes a real sense -- no longer slides off). Cannot yet draw-and-keep or wield it: housing into ember flesh fails (wrong vessel); needs an EXTERNAL ember-housed vessel. Counter 1/10 toward Force Manipulation. Bias +1 per the ember-parallel ladder, LATENT until he has a vessel to act through.", "ladder": "affinity", "source": "TURN 80: first contact-draw of the winding-drum core's wound stored-force, reached by MATCHING the essence's kinetic nature -- spun his own body holding the core to touch a motion-essence through motion (INT 20 + intent 5 + bias 0 + roll 11, DC 17, margin 19). The rotational vector WORKED -- first genuine contact, foreign axis 0->1. His destination (pull it into myself) FAILED: stored-force will not set in single-pole ember flesh (Ember-Tempered Body sink-not-source; t62 cold-into-flesh NO, reaffirmed) -- drew it, retained nothing, it sluiced through and out. Backlash: stamina -12 + focus -8 + recoil-stagger (no HP-burn). TAUGHT: the essence is reachable, the BODY is the wrong vessel -- bind it into an external vessel (ember-house the core), not pull it into himself.", "counter": 1}], "attributes": {"LUCK": 11, "WILL": 20, "MIGHT": 14, "FINESSE": 14, "PRESENCE": 16, "VITALITY": 12, "INTELLECT": 20, "PERCEPTION": 12}, "_derivedHint": "HP, Stamina, Focus, Initiative, defenses computed by engine/engine.ts from attributes + equipment.", "attributePointsUnspent": 3},"id":"3d3718b1-3fd3-5d7a-a763-4aa67695533a"}
-{"externalId": "floor-05", "kind": "floor", "sheet": {"name": "The False Haven", "exits": ["the haven's 'onward door' is ILLUSORY (part of the false gallery); the REAL ascending stair is behind it and appears only when the haven collapses — i.e. when the Host's true form falls. No honest exit exists until the floor is solved; the floor cannot be walked past."], "floor": 5, "rooms": [{"id": "haven-threshold", "desc": "The mouth of the haven, where the exit-stair from the dark shaft gives onto warm gold light. From here — without stepping in — you can see the near length of the long room: the laid table, the banked hearth across it, soft furniture along the warm wall, the hooded figure rising by the fire. Beyond it the haven continues — a second warmer hall, and more past that, the gold light receding back further than seems possible for a single floor. It is everything floor four was not: warm, lit, safe, kind. That is exactly the problem, if you let yourself think it.", "name": "The Threshold", "light": "Abundant, GOLD, FALSE. Hearth and lamps light warmly but sourceless — no heat, no honest shadows. Inverts floor 4 (there real light was scarce vs dark; here false light is everywhere and Alan's ONE REAL FLAME — Ember / a spark / Burning Anger's banked core — is the only TRUE light, thus the verification tool). This matters MORE the deeper he goes, as the haven fakes the cheaper tells and only real fire stays honest.", "water": "The ewer offers what looks like clear water/wine — PART OF THE LURE (illusory sustenance; 'drinking' lowers guard, not hydration). NO honest potable water on this floor — pre-decided contrast with floor 2 (real water). Do not confabulate a seep; the comfort is all surface.", "exhausted": "A second threshold read yields the same tells clearer, not new ones. To learn more he must commit inside (and the truth gets more dangerous as he does). The threshold is safe to stand and read; one step in begins the haven's hold. RETREAT down to floor 4's stilled headworks is open from here.", "otherExits": "back DOWN to floor 4's headworks (open — retreat possible); FORWARD into the Hall of Welcome", "scoutReveal": {"_note": "BESPOKE field — Alan ended his action on a quiet scout from the threshold. Tiers what a recon read surfaces. Resolve his scout by read quality: a passive look (his WEAK PER axis) buys the LIE; a reasoned INT read (his PEAK axis) buys the tells; his iron WILL is a third sense. The deeper floor stays held-dark until he commits.", "heldDark": "NOT surfaced by the scout (revealed only by committing, room by room): that the haven is a deep predation gallery of FIVE rooms; that the deception COMPOUNDS inward (each room the illusion learns to fake the tell that exposed it in the last — first it has no shadows, then it fakes shadows, then heat, then reflections — forcing Alan to climb a verification ladder: shadow → Ember heat-shadow → reflection → cross-referencing several tells at once); that there are MULTIPLE glamour-predators (a lone Welcomer, then a coordinated PAIR), not one; that the 'host' is the warden weaving it all, and the boss is STAGED — identify the real one among decoys, THEN it drops the haven and its true predator-form is a fast, genuinely lethal fight, THEN the collapsing haven is its own escape hazard. The scout earns Alan grounds to DISTRUST and a read of HOW the floor lies — not the map of what's inside.", "passiveLook": "A glance / tired PER read returns a genuine haven — safe room, warm meal, kind host, rest. Nothing visibly wrong. (PER 12 is his weak axis, Sensitivity-not-Observance — a passive spot does NOT pierce this. Reward reasoning, never noticing.)", "intReconRead_modest": "A deliberate INT read (intent ~4-6) surfaces ONE-TWO tells: (1) THE HEARTH GLOWS BUT THROWS NO HEAT — and Alan, Ember-attuned, feels the ABSENCE of real heat like a missing note in a chord. (2) The 'steaming' ewer and plates: the steam doesn't move with the air; nothing has cooled or been touched. Presentation, not substance.", "intReconRead_strong": "A strong INT read (intent 7+), or one that checks the FLOOR and SHADOWS instead of the figures: the false light is SOURCELESS — hearth, lamps, and the hooded figure cast no honest shadow, while Alan's own body does. The host's welcome gesture REPEATS on a faint loop. Under the table-cloth edges: old bones, dressed over. His WILL (17) registers the pull-to-relax as FOREIGN — a comfort pressed on him from outside, not his own. AND the read of DEPTH: the haven runs back too far for one floor — there is more here than the threshold shows, and it gets warmer (more convincing) the deeper it goes, not less."}, "searchables": [{"use": "an echo / projection of the floor's warden. Open empty hands, warm voice, no weapon. TIER-1 TELL: casts no honest shadow, gesture repeats, warmth is sourceless. Striking the IMAGE does almost nothing (the real Host is deep in the haven; this is a projection). Reasoning about it (INT) or holding real flame to it (Ember) reveals it as image.", "note": "the scout centerpiece. A reader reads WHY the figure is wrong; he does not swing at a projection from the door.", "thing": "the hooded host-figure by the hearth (rising to greet)"}, {"use": "the lure's set-dressing. Food LOOKS fresh, never steams right, never cools, never depletes. Under the cloth: old bones. EATING/DRINKING here is the trap — accepting the haven (lowers guard, deepens the hold). No honest sustenance.", "note": "pre-decided: the meal is bait. 'Is the food real?' = no, and taking it is the wrong move.", "thing": "the long laid table (steaming ewer, plates, pushed-back chairs)"}, {"use": "THE personalized tell. Glows warm, lights the room, radiates NO heat — an Ember-attuned reader feels the absence acutely (a fire that gives nothing screams wrongness to a heat-sense). Casts no shadow. The clearest single proof, keyed to ALAN — his build is the floor's lie-detector.", "note": "his Ember = the verification instrument for the whole floor (like floor 2's brazier / floor 4's lantern). It is also the FIRST rung of the verification ladder the deeper floor will keep raising.", "thing": "the banked hearth (across the room)"}, {"use": "the honest read-surface. Real things displace dust and throw a shadow in the gold light; woven images do neither. A reader who watches the FLOOR and the SHADOWS rather than the inviting figures sees which presences are real — the general key to every illusion here (until the floor learns to fake it deeper in).", "note": "rewards INT/method over PER/noticing. NOTE for the coordinator: this tell WORKS at the threshold and the hall, then the haven learns to fake shadows — see the verification ladder in designerNotes.", "thing": "the threshold floor — dust, and what casts a shadow"}, {"use": "an ILLUSORY exit — part of the gallery. Promises an easy way up past the meal; walking 'through' it loops back. The REAL ascending stair is behind it and appears only when the Host's true form falls. The floor cannot be skipped.", "note": "the bypass-trap: the floor must be solved, not passed.", "thing": "the 'onward door' far down the haven (warm light beyond it)", "status": "ILLUSORY — resolves to real stair only on clearing"}]}, {"id": "hall-of-welcome", "desc": "Past the threshold the haven wraps around you — warmth on all sides, the table at your elbow, soft couches and a made bed pulling at days of exhaustion. A figure waits here, nearer and warmer than the first: a fellow climber by the look — or unsettlingly like a face you'd be glad to see — with a flask, a clean cloth, and real concern. 'You're bleeding. Let me. Sit down, just for a moment.' Every word is the thing you most want to hear. And the tells from the threshold are quieter here — this figure DOES throw a shadow.", "name": "The Hall of Welcome", "light": "False gold; the Welcomer now casts a (faked) shadow. Alan's Ember held to it gives the heat-shadow tell that the plain shadow no longer can.", "water": "NONE honest (the Welcomer's flask is lure).", "exhausted": "Once note and remains are taken and the Welcomer resolved, the hall holds only false furnishings (lures, not loot). No farming; the bed never becomes safe.", "otherExits": "back to the threshold (and down to floor 4); forward to the Long Gallery", "searchables": [{"use": "the lesser warden — bait wearing kindness. Its 'aid' (letting it tend you, taking its flask, sitting) is the kill: at full-dropped guard it strikes intimate and lethal. Presents harmless, READS harmless to PER. TIER-2 TELL (the ladder's first escalation): the threshold's shadow-tell FAILS here — the haven has learned to fake shadows — so the honest tell is now the EMBER HEAT-SHADOW: under his real flame, only a real body throws a heat-warped shadow; the glamour throws a cold one. Striking the PRESENTED figure ×0.25; the REVEALED true form ×1.8.", "note": "the floor's 'front-loaded lethality' beat (Stalker-equivalent) — through TRUST, and now also the first proof that the verification ladder ESCALATES (shadow defeated → Ember heat-shadow). A reader who relied on plain shadows must climb a rung.", "thing": "The Welcomer (offering aid/rest)"}, {"use": "THE lure, pre-decided as a kill. Lying down = you do not wake (the haven feeds on a guard fully dropped to sleep). NO real rest / HP-recovery on this floor. 'Can I heal up here?' = NO; trying is the trap.", "note": "decided fail-state, not recovery. Do not narrate genuine rest.", "thing": "the rest-couches and the made bed", "status": "INTACT — untriggered"}, {"use": "weak-PER COMPENSATION (the floor-3 wall-note / floor-4 corpse-note pattern). The note, scratched into the floorboard: 'DON'T EAT. DON'T SLEEP. DON'T LET THE KIND ONES TOUCH YOU. THEY LEARN YOUR TRICKS — IT FAKES THE SHADOWS NOW, IT'LL FAKE MORE. ONLY YOUR OWN FIRE STAYS HONEST. THE REAL ONE IS DEEP IN, AT THE HEAD OF THE TABLE. KILL IT TWICE.' Hands a reader the verification-ladder logic, the lures, where the Host is, AND the staged-boss warning ('kill it twice') — fair pay for weak PER.", "note": "the lore-gate; names the compounding deception and the two-phase boss plainly. Reaching it requires having come inside past the Welcomer's offer.", "thing": "a previous climber's remains (behind the couches) + a scrawled note", "status": "INTACT"}]}, {"id": "the-long-gallery", "desc": "The haven opens into a long mirrored gallery — silvered glass down both walls, a second table, more hearths, and TWO welcoming figures this time, moving to either side of you with the same warm concern: one pressing a cup, one circling to your back 'to look at that wound.' The warmth here has WEIGHT — you'd swear you feel the hearth's heat on your skin now. The tells are getting harder to keep.", "name": "The Long Gallery", "light": "False gold WITH faked heat now (he feels it). Only the mirrors and his own fire stay honest. A thrown Ember flare reflects truly in the glass; the figures cast no reflection in it.", "water": "NONE honest.", "exhausted": "Once the pair is resolved, the gallery holds only mirrors (tools, not loot) and the cold seam (a path, not a prize). No respawn-farming.", "otherExits": "back to the Hall of Welcome; forward (following the cold) to the Deep Den", "searchables": [{"use": "a COORDINATED PAIR (multi-threat — see encounter the-welcomers-pair-01). One holds his attention with the offer; the other flanks for the intimate kill. TIER-3 TELL: the Ember heat-shadow tell now FAILS too — the gallery fakes heat (you feel the hearth; the figures feel warm). The honest tell becomes the MIRRORS: a real body throws a reflection; the woven figures do NOT. He must read the silvered glass, not his senses.", "note": "the ladder's second escalation (heat defeated → reflection) AND the threat ramp: two predators that sandwich him is meaningfully harder than floor 4's lone Stalker. A reader keeps his back to a mirror or a wall and refuses to be flanked.", "thing": "the two Welcomers (one fronting with aid, one circling behind)"}, {"use": "the TIER-3 verification tool. Real presences reflect; glamours don't. Catching a figure in the glass is a clean real-vs-projected test that bypasses his fooled senses — and lets him see a flanker coming (countering his weak PER with reasoning + geometry).", "note": "give a reader who uses the mirrors an honest edge against the pair and forward into the den/boss. Also foreshadows the reflection-faking of the next room.", "thing": "the silvered gallery mirrors (both walls)"}, {"use": "a real, faint cold draft from BEHIND the illusion — the only honestly cold thing on a floor of fake warmth. Following it (INT to trust the cold over the fake heat) leads truer-inward than the looping 'onward door' — a navigation tell that the real structure is colder and barer than the gold haven pretends.", "note": "the honest cold = the real den bleeding through. Rewards trusting a tell over comfort; threads toward the deep den / boss.", "thing": "a cold draft seam (low on one mirrored wall)"}]}, {"id": "the-deep-den", "desc": "The gold thins. This room is colder, the welcome threadbare — the illusion working harder over something it can barely cover. There are figures here too, and now they throw shadows AND reflections, and the air is warm where they stand. Every single tell you climbed to is being faked at once. Under the fraying gold you catch the real room beneath: bare wet stone, a midden of what the haven has eaten — packs, boots, bones, a long time's worth of climbers who sat down to rest.", "name": "The Deep Den", "light": "Threadbare gold over real cold dark. Here the false light is failing — patches of the real dim den show through. His Ember is both verification AND, increasingly, the only real light, easing back toward the floor-4 dynamic as the haven thins.", "water": "ONE honest drink — the scavenged flask in the midden (real water, hidden under the illusion; one use). Everywhere else the offered water is lure. Pre-decided: the only true water on the floor is the reward for reaching the cold truth.", "exhausted": "Once the cache is taken and the figures resolved, the den holds only the midden and the bleed-through stone. No farming; the real water is one-and-done.", "otherExits": "back to the Long Gallery; forward / down-slope to the Host's Seat", "searchables": [{"use": "TIER-4: NO single tell works anymore. The den fakes shadow, heat, AND reflection. The honest read is now CROSS-REFERENCE + BEHAVIOR: woven figures loop (repeat micro-gestures on a cycle), they don't displace the dust/grit underfoot, and they cannot answer a CHANGE he introduces (step unexpectedly and the real one tracks late; the projections are on rails). A reader stops trusting any one sense and triangulates — 2-of-3 disagreeing tells (a looping gesture + undisturbed dust + a beat-late reaction) marks a projection. This is a DEDUCTION, not a spot-check.", "note": "the ladder's top rung before the boss: the floor has defeated each individual tell, so the complexity becomes triangulation. This is the new-axis payoff — reading is now genuinely hard, not a one-line weakness.", "thing": "the figures here (shadowed, reflected, warm — every tell faked)"}, {"use": "the stakes, and a real-supply cache. Among the eaten: usable scavenge — a flask of REAL water (the only honest water on the floor, here, hidden under the lie — one drink), a spare iron spike (atk 3 offhand), and a half-burned journal whose last legible line: 'IT WEARS THE ROOM. WHEN YOU KILL THE HOST THE WHOLE PLACE DIES AT ONCE — AND THE FLOOR GOES WITH IT. BE NEAR THE STAIR WHEN IT DOES.' Foreshadows phase-3 (the collapse) and hands him the real water as fair reward for reaching the bleak-through.", "note": "the honest cache under the illusion: a reader who pushed through the comfort to the cold truth is rewarded (one real drink + the phase-3 warning). Counterpart to the lures of the warm rooms — truth is colder and barer but real.", "thing": "the midden of prior climbers (under the fraying gold)", "status": "INTACT"}, {"use": "the floor's truth bleeding through — the den is a cold stone predation-chamber the haven is painted over. The real geometry is tighter and barer than the gold pretends, and it slopes toward the Host's seat. Reading the real stone (where the dust lies undisturbed, where the cold comes from) navigates truer than the warm illusion. It also shows the floor is structurally REAL stone — phase-3's collapse is the ILLUSION dying, not the stone, but the illusion was hiding the room's edges (a real drop at the chamber's lip — a floor-4 falling callback, compounded).", "note": "the real layer. Decided: the stone is real; the gold is the lie; phase-3 strips the gold and the hidden edges/drop become live hazards.", "thing": "the bare wet stone beneath the gold (the real den)"}]}, {"id": "the-hosts-seat", "desc": "The gold gathers itself for one last, best lie: a high-backed chair at the head of the long table, and in it the Host — the gracious one, hands folded, smiling like he has all the time in the world and is pleased you came so far. This is the loom of the whole haven. When you raise a weapon he does not flinch — he MULTIPLIES: five of him around the table, then seven, every one identical, every one casting a shadow, every one warm, every one reflected, every one saying come, sit, you've earned it. Strike the wrong one and the others are still smiling while you bleed. And the note said it: kill it twice.", "name": "The Host's Seat", "light": "False gold thickest here (the Host is its source) through phase 1; then it DIES with the true form, leaving only Alan's Ember and the dim honest stone for phases 2-3. Light-discipline is the through-line of the back half.", "water": "NONE.", "exhausted": "After the true form falls and the haven collapses, the seat is bare predation-den stone, the real remains of everyone it took, the drop at the lip, and the open stair. Nothing respawns; the floor is cleared.", "otherExits": "the real ascending stair ahead (on clearing); the den behind", "searchables": [{"use": "the floor boss — STAGED (see encounters the-host-01 phase 1 + the-host-trueform-02 phase 2). PHASE 1 is the IDENTIFICATION fight: every decoy now fakes EVERY cheap tell (shadow, heat, reflection), so the plain tools are spent — the real one is found only by (a) his EMBER FLARE / salting the room with real fire, which reveals all projections at once for a turn, plus (b) the den's triangulation (the real Host loops least, displaces dust, sits truly at the head where the slope bottoms). Striking a decoy ×0.25 + the real Host counters (~67). A confirmed true-Host strike ×3 doesn't kill it — it CRACKS the haven.", "note": "phase 1 = the hardest read on the floor (all tells faked at once). The Ember-flare + cross-reference is the intended solve; the note ('bring your own fire', 'kill it twice') primes both.", "thing": "The Host (at the head of the table) and his ring of decoys"}, {"use": "PHASE 2 — the ×3 true-strike doesn't end it; it tears the gracious mask off and the thing under all the faces stands up: a fast, lean predator (see the-host-trueform-02). The gold dies; the room goes to real cold stone. Now it is a STRAIGHT, dangerous fight — it acts before Alan (Init 33), hits for ~94 of his 124 HP per connect, and tries to slip into the failing shadows to re-cloak. GATE here is LIGHT-DISCIPLINE (a floor-4 callback): pinned in Alan's Ember-light it takes ×1.5 (~2 clean hits drop it); if it reaches shadow it flickers half-real at ×0.5 and re-hides. He must keep it lit and finish fast.", "note": "phase 2 = the difficulty ramp — a real kill-risk fight, not a puzzle. Reading won phase 1; survival + light-discipline win phase 2.", "thing": "the Host's TRUE FORM (revealed when the haven cracks)"}, {"use": "PHASE 3 — when the true form falls, the whole illusion dies AT ONCE (the journal warned it): the gold peels away, and with it the painted-over floor — the real den's edges and the drop at the chamber's lip (hidden by the lie this whole time) are suddenly live. A brief escape beat: reach the real ascending stair (now revealed where the 'onward door' pretended to be) before the dying illusion drops the false footing. A reader who heeded the journal stays NEAR THE STAIR for the kill and steps onto solid stone as the gold falls away.", "note": "phase 3 = staged climax, not a third enemy: a short environmental escape compounding floor-4's falling onto floor-5's deception. Heeding the journal ('be near the stair') trivializes it; ignoring it risks a fall on the win.", "thing": "the failing haven / the chamber's hidden edges (PHASE 3)", "status": "real stair revealed on clearing"}]}], "scale": "FLOOR 5 IS A STEP UP IN SIZE (5 rooms vs floor 4's 3) AND COMPLEXITY (a COMPOUNDING verification ladder — each room the illusion defeats the tell that beat the last, forcing Alan up a rung of proof — plus MULTI-THREAT encounters and a STAGED multi-phase boss). See designerNotes → ESCALATION and floors/SCHEMA.md → 'Escalation mandate'. This is deliberately not the floor-4 template; the shape is varied as well as the axis.", "theme": "You climb the last of the dark shaft and the Tower changes its mind about you. The cold updraft warms. The grey seam at the top opens not onto more stone but onto a long, low room lit gold — lamplight, a banked hearth, the smell of bread and woodsmoke after days of dust and grease. A table is laid down its length, plates and a steaming ewer, chairs pushed back as if a meal just paused. Couches and a made bed wait along the warm wall. By the hearth a figure rises — hooded soft, both hands open and empty, a voice like someone glad you finally made it: 'You're hurt. Come in, climber. Sit. You've earned the rest.' After floor four's killing dark, every nerve you own wants to walk in and put the weapon down. And this is only the threshold — the haven runs back and back, room after warm room, deeper than one glance can hold. (Continuity: reached by ASCENDING from floor 4's headworks. Alan ends his action on a QUIET SCOUT from the threshold — he has NOT committed inside. Resolve the scout against scoutReveal in the first room. Do NOT narrate the haven as real or safe in the System voice; the warmth and welcome are the player-facing surface only.)", "encounters": [{"id": "the-welcomer-01", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "The Welcomer", "class": "Glamour-predator", "level": 4, "hpNote": "engine: VIT8(64)+MIGHT2(18) = 82 HP. physDef (8+14)/2 = 11. physAtk 9*1.5+14+3 = 30.5. Init 13+14 = 27 (beats Alan's 26 on the trust-opener — front-load that turn). Threat = the trust-ambush, not HP.", "rollMode": "2d10", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 0}, "weapon": {"atk": 3}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 8, "WILL": 13, "MIGHT": 9, "FINESSE": 14, "PRESENCE": 16, "VITALITY": 8, "INTELLECT": 14, "PERCEPTION": 13}, "baseDamage": 14, "intentTypical": 2, "readableTrait": "A slight, cold predator wearing a kind climber's face (PRESENCE 16 / FINESSE 14 sell it; frail — 82 HP, no armor). GATE — TRUST is the danger (the social mirror of floor 4's dark). Its weapon is the WELCOME: if Alan accepts aid / sits / lets it close, it strikes intimate from full trust — coordinator: opening blow at intent 6-8 vs a flat-footed Alan (~53-70 to his 124 HP, and it presses before he recovers; not the VIT-6 near-kill the Stalker was, but brutal and spiraling if he keeps trusting). Striking the PRESENTED kind figure ×0.25 (a woven image). It is REVEALED by the TIER-2 tell — the plain shadow-tell is faked here, so use the EMBER HEAT-SHADOW (real flame shows a real body's heat-warped shadow; the glamour's is cold) — or by the mirrors deeper in; the true cold form then takes ×1.8 and his INT read of its real lunge earns intent 8+. The wrong read — taking it at its word, the flask, the seat — gets him knifed from arm's reach. It mirrors a face he WANTS to trust; a reader trusts no one the haven hands him, and refuses every comfort."}, "reward": {"drop": "a false-face shard (glamour/illusion-affinity seed — woven light holding a borrowed face) and its true hide (thin, cold, light-drinking like the Stalker's lens — crafting material toward a concealing garment)"}, "trigger": "accepting the Welcomer's aid/rest in the Hall of Welcome, OR moving deeper, OR revealing/striking it"}, {"id": "the-welcomers-pair-01", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "The Welcomers (coordinated pair — run TWO instances of this sheet)", "class": "Glamour-predator (pair)", "level": 4, "hpNote": "engine (each): VIT8(64)+MIGHT2(18) = 82 HP. physDef 11. physAtk 30.5. Init 27 each. TWO of them = the floor-5 threat step-up; the danger is the flank + the trust, not a HP wall.", "rollMode": "2d10", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 0}, "weapon": {"atk": 3}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 8, "WILL": 13, "MIGHT": 9, "FINESSE": 14, "PRESENCE": 16, "VITALITY": 8, "INTELLECT": 14, "PERCEPTION": 13}, "baseDamage": 14, "intentTypical": 3, "readableTrait": "TWO Welcomers (same sheet, run as two) working as a MULTI-THREAT pair — the genuine difficulty ramp over floor 4's lone predator. One FRONTS (holds attention with the cup/offer), one FLANKS (circles to his back 'to look at the wound') for the intimate kill; if he fixates on one, the other lands the trust-strike (~53-70). GATE: same as the lone Welcomer (presented ×0.25 / revealed true form ×1.8 / trust-opener lethal), but now the TIER-3 tell — the Ember heat-shadow is ALSO faked in the gallery, so the honest tool is the MIRRORS (woven figures throw no reflection). The read: keep his back to a mirror or wall (deny the flank — geometry beating his weak PER), catch each figure in the glass to tell real-from-projected, refuse both offers, and reveal/strike the true forms. Brute-trading in the open while flanked is a lethal slog; a reader controls the angles and uses the silver. Coordinator: the pair can be split (lure one past a mirror, isolate it) — reward that."}, "reward": {"drop": "two false-face shards (a matched pair — a glamour-craft seed toward casting a borrowed face of his own) and a silvered gallery-shard (a true-reflection lens — a verification tool he can carry forward against illusion)"}, "trigger": "entering the Long Gallery / engaging either of the two figures (they act together)"}, {"id": "the-host-01", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "The Host (Warden of the Haven) — Phase 1, the Weaver", "class": "Gallery Warden", "level": 5, "hpNote": "engine: VIT8(120)+MIGHT2(24) = 144 HP. physDef (15+10)/2+2 = 14.5. physAtk 12*1.5+10+4 = 32. Init 12+10 = 22 (Alan's 26 first, but worthless until he's IDed the real one). HP a wall only if you brute the decoys.", "rollMode": "2d10", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 2}, "weapon": {"atk": 4}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 6, "WILL": 14, "MIGHT": 12, "FINESSE": 10, "PRESENCE": 17, "VITALITY": 15, "INTELLECT": 16, "PERCEPTION": 12}, "baseDamage": 18, "intentTypical": 3, "readableTrait": "The loom of the false haven, 144 HP — phase 1 is IDENTIFICATION, not HP. Threatened, it SPLITS into identical decoys (5, then 7) ringing the table, and — unlike the rooms before — each decoy now fakes EVERY cheap tell at once (shadow, heat, reflection), because the haven has climbed the whole ladder with him. So the plain tools are spent. The real one is found by: (a) his EMBER FLARE / salting the room with real fire — reveals ALL projections at once for a turn (coordinator: the true-Host strike that turn is at intent +2 and UNMITIGATED), and (b) the den's triangulation (the real Host loops least, displaces dust/grit, and sits truly at the head where the floor slopes down). Striking any decoy ×0.25 (~22-25/hit on 144) AND each wrong strike the real Host lands an intimate counter (~67 to Alan's 124 — two wrong reads is near-death) and reshuffles. A confirmed true-Host strike ×3 (~299) does NOT kill it — it CRACKS the haven and triggers PHASE 2 (the note: 'kill it twice'). WILL-gate (his second-best axis, load-bearing): the haven pulls steadily to relax/trust/do-nothing; his iron WILL (mentDef 35.5) makes him resistant IF he leans on it — a reader recognizes the comfort as foreign and acts. Brute-clearing seven decoys is a counter-stacked slog that kills him first."}, "reward": {"drop": "(phase 1 banks no reward on its own — the cracked haven flows directly into phase 2; reward is on the true-form kill)"}, "trigger": "raising a weapon to the Host / forcing the false exit (PHASE 1 — the decoy-weaver)"}, {"id": "the-host-trueform-02", "enemy": {"kind": "enemy", "name": "The Host — Phase 2, True Form", "class": "Haven-predator (unmasked)", "level": 5, "hpNote": "engine: VIT8(104)+MIGHT2(26) = 130 HP. physDef (13+17)/2+1 = 16. physAtk 13*1.5+17+5 = 41.5. Init 16+17 = 33 (acts before Alan's 26 — the core of the threat). 1d20 Wild Variance = real spike risk both ways.", "rollMode": "1d20", "equipment": {"armor": {"def": 1}, "weapon": {"atk": 5}}, "attributes": {"LUCK": 7, "WILL": 15, "MIGHT": 13, "FINESSE": 17, "PRESENCE": 8, "VITALITY": 13, "INTELLECT": 16, "PERCEPTION": 16}, "baseDamage": 20, "intentTypical": 4, "readableTrait": "The thing under all the faces — fast and lean, 130 HP, the gracious mask gone (PRESENCE crashes to 8; FINESSE 17 / PERCEPTION 16 / Init 33 — it acts BEFORE Alan now). This is the DIFFICULTY RAMP: phase 1 was a read, phase 2 is a real, lethal fight. It hits for ~94 of Alan's 124 HP per clean connect (1d20 — swingy, crits ~5%), so TWO connects kill him and it strikes first — he cannot trade slowly. GATE is LIGHT-DISCIPLINE (a floor-4 callback, compounded): the haven is dead so there's no decoy game, but the predator tries to slip into the failing shadows to re-cloak and reset. Pinned in Alan's EMBER-LIGHT it is fully real and exposed — coordinator ×1.5 (~126/hit, ~2 clean hits drop it); if it reaches shadow it flickers half-real — coordinator ×0.5 (~42/hit) and re-hides for a beat (resetting toward another ambush). The line: keep it LIT (Burning Anger's banked core, an Ember flare, a thrown brand), corner it against real stone, and finish in two before it lands two. Aelwyn, if present, fronts it (her HP/physDef soak the ~94 blows so Alan can place the killing strikes from light) — but solo is winnable by light-discipline + his glass-cannon output."}, "reward": {"drop": "the haven's ANCHOR (a 'lantern of true seeing' / revelation-core — a cold clear lens that, lit with his Ember, shows woven illusion for what it is; a strong forward counter-tool for future deception floors + a true-sight affinity seed) and the Host's mantle (the woven-light cloak — glamour-craft material / a PRESENCE-keyed deception-affinity seed)"}, "trigger": "a confirmed true-Host strike cracks the haven (PHASE 2 — the predator under the faces; flows straight from the-host-01)"}], "designerNotes": "FLOOR 5 — the DECEPTION / VERIFICATION floor, AND the first floor built to the whole-tower ESCALATION mandate (Alan, 2026-06-24). Two things at once: a NEW tactical axis (novelty) and a clear STEP UP in size/complexity/difficulty (magnitude). See floors/SCHEMA.md → 'Escalation mandate' for the curve this floor seeds.\n\nNEW AXIS (novelty, continuing f1 chokepoint / f2 water / f3 acoustics / f4 dark+timing+falling): TRUST vs VERIFICATION — what Alan perceives is unreliable; the floor is solved by reasoning real-from-false and refusing comfort, not by force or noticing. The welcome IS the weapon; a deliberate tonal swerve after floor 4's killing dark.\n\nMAGNITUDE (the new mandate — how floor 5 is bigger/harder than floor 4, not just different):\n- SIZE: 5 rooms vs floor 4's 3 (threshold → hall → long gallery → deep den → host's seat).\n- COMPOUNDING MECHANIC (the complexity engine): a VERIFICATION LADDER. The deception LEARNS — each room it fakes the tell that beat it in the last, forcing Alan up a rung of proof: threshold = no shadows (tell: shadow/Ember) → hall = fakes shadows (tell: Ember heat-shadow) → gallery = fakes heat (tell: mirror reflection) → den = fakes reflection (tell: cross-reference/triangulation — loop + dust + beat-late reaction) → boss = fakes everything at once (solve: Ember-FLARE reveal + triangulation). This is layered/compounding, not one static gimmick — the read gets genuinely harder as he climbs.\n- MULTI-THREAT: not one warden + one gimmick. A lone Welcomer (hall), then a COORDINATED PAIR that flanks (gallery), then the staged boss. Threat ramps from single → pair → staged-multiphase.\n- STAGED BOSS (3 phases): phase 1 IDENTIFICATION (read the real Host among 7 all-tells-faked decoys — the hardest read on the floor) → phase 2 TRUE-FORM FIGHT (the ×3 strike cracks, doesn't kill; a fast predator that acts first and ~94/hit nearly two-shots Alan — a real survival fight gated on LIGHT-DISCIPLINE, a floor-4 callback) → phase 3 COLLAPSE-ESCAPE (the dying haven strips the painted-over floor; reach the revealed stair before the false footing drops — floor-4 falling compounded onto floor-5 deception). 'Kill it twice' (the note) = the staged shape, fairly telegraphed.\n\nBUILT ON ALAN'S L6 PROFILE (sheets/alan.json): PUNISHES weak PERCEPTION (passive look buys the lie — Sensitivity-not-Observance fails), REWARDS peak INTELLECT (20 — every tell reasoning-discoverable; the den is pure deduction). Two traits made load-bearing in new ways: (1) EMBER AFFINITY = the floor's lie-detector and the one tell the ladder can never fully fake (real fire stays honest), keyed to HIS build like floor 2's brazier / floor 4's lantern; (2) iron WILL (17, mentDef 35.5 — a fortress) = a DETECTION SENSE (the comfort-pull reads as foreign to a will that strong). NOTE his mentDef is too high for a mind-ATTACK floor to threaten — so the floor deliberately does NOT roll ment attacks; it lies to his senses and lures his CHOICES (eat/rest/trust), which no defense stat blocks. New boss-SHAPE too: f3 (keystone) and f4 (pawl) were 'strike the one KNOWN weak point' (placement puzzles); f5 phase 1 is an IDENTIFICATION puzzle ('which of seven identical is REAL?'), phase 2 a straight fight — varied shape, same 'reading beats brute force' spine.\n\nDAMAGE-GATE MODEL (continued f2-4, REQUIRED): each readableTrait carries explicit gate ×M applied to baseDamage before margin-scaling. Floor 5 gates: Welcomer ×0.25 glamour / ×1.8 revealed (+ trust-ambush ~53-70); Pair same + flank pressure; Host phase-1 ×0.25 decoy (+ ~67 counter/wrong strike) / ×3 true-Host (cracks, not kills) / Ember-flare reveal = intent +2 unmitigated; Host phase-2 ×1.5 light-pinned / ×0.5 if it reaches shadow. VERIFIED EMPIRICALLY vs engine/engine.ts on the LIVE L6 sheet (physAtk 45 w/ Burning Anger, physDef 14 w/ cloak, 1d20): Host decoy ×0.25 ~22-25/hit vs 144 (slog) w/ ~67 counters; true-Host ×3 ~299 (cracks the haven); Welcomer glamour ×0.25 ~20 / true ×1.8 ~143; true-form pinned ×1.5 ~126/hit (~2 to drop 130 HP) vs shadow ×0.5 ~42; true-form INTO Alan ~94/hit vs 124 HP acting first (Init 33) — two connects kill him. The math enforces it: read + refuse comfort + light-discipline win; force-or-trust is lethal.\n\nPOWER BUDGET / DIFFICULTY: L6 with Burning Anger (atk 10, banked ember core — his own fire is always on hand, which is WHY the Ember-verification line is reliably available), Stalker cloak (physDef 14), HP 124, Focus 114, mentDef 35.5. A strong glass-cannon; the floor doesn't threaten his HP wall in the read phases (it threatens his JUDGMENT) but the phase-2 true-form genuinely CAN kill him (the ramp). Net difficulty: a clear step up from floor 4 — bigger, layered, multi-threat, and with a real-kill-risk boss phase. Built winnable SOLO; COMPANION NOTE (coordinator's call, none written in): a 'two minds see the lie' floor is a natural companion-entry beat — an ally who throws a real shadow is itself a verification anchor and fronts the true-form's ~94 blows — flagged to Alan as optional, not required.\n\nSEQUENCING / LETHAL TRAPS: (a) TRUSTING — eat/drink/sit/sleep/accept aid: the haven feeds on a dropped guard, the Welcomers knife from arm's reach; (b) FORCING — hacking decoys/phantoms: counter-stacked slog; (c) phase-2 CARELESSNESS — trading slowly with the true form or letting it reach shadow: it two-shots him. The floor pivots on the SCOUT he just took (distrust from the threshold) and on never relaxing inward. RETREAT is open at the threshold (down to floor 4); committing inside begins the hold. LOOP NOTE (coordinator-only): layout, the ladder, searchables, and all enemy sheets are FIXED/reproducible; the held-dark loop context is iris-manager's — nothing secret is in this floor's math. NO honest water except the one scavenged midden flask; NO real rest/heal (decided contrasts — the haven only offers the APPEARANCE; do not confabulate real sustenance). REWARD PATH: a glamour seed + true-hide (Welcomer), a matched glamour pair + a true-reflection lens (the pair), and the haven's ANCHOR — a 'lantern of true seeing' that lit with his Ember unmakes illusion (a strong forward counter-tool, hooking future deception floors) + a deception/PRESENCE mantle (the Host). Feeds Equipment/Crafting, Affinities, and the still-latent social/PRESENCE axis. SCOUT-REVEAL (haven-threshold → scoutReveal) is the live deliverable; the deeper rooms/staged boss are prepped and held-dark until he commits.\n\nLENS RULING (locked t71, 2026-06-24): looking THROUGH the Stalker eye-lenses (light-DRINKING dark-hunter eyes) at the threshold DRINKS the false gold and turns his deduced strong-read into direct SIGHT of the honest substrate (dead cold hearth, true dimness, bones plain, host-figure thinning to a HOLLOW PROJECTION — NOT the held-dark phase-2 true form). BOUNDS: threshold line-of-sight only (no seeing into deeper rooms/pair/boss); the lens is a LIGHT-SUBTRACTING tool — decisive here (the threshold lie is purely light) but NOT a master key (the deeper ladder fakes shadow/heat/reflection/behavior, which drinking light doesn't expose and can obscure). CONSEQUENCE: CLEAN, no provocation — the lens ABSORBS (a stealth organ), unlike the t57 emberlight beacon that EMITTED and drew the Stalker; don't aggro on it. Tradeoff is INSTRUMENT ANTAGONISM not threat — it drinks TRUE light too (his Ember), dimming his own lie-detector while worn and fighting Ember-flare deeper where that's the solve (self-limiting). REWARD ARC: the eye-lens is the deliberate PRECURSOR to the Host's 'lantern of true seeing' — lens = crude/passive/SUBTRACTS false light (half-blinds to true light); lantern = refined/Ember-lit/ADDS true sight with no blindness cost. Kept distinct.\n\nGRAPPLE/TETHER RULING (locked t72, 2026-06-24): throwing a chain-tether from the threshold to drag the haven's furniture out without entering — PHYSICS INVARIANT (lens-independent): the hook passes THROUGH the glamour-feast (light, not matter) and catches only the REAL substrate beneath (the charnel bones); host-image never reacts. GEOGRAPHY: only the NEAR end of the table/charnel is within tether reach of the threshold-stone; hearth/host's-seat/deeper hall are SET DEEP, beyond any throw without a step in — depth requires committing, the grapple is a threshold-edge salvage tool, never a strip-from-outside exploit. THREAT: CLEAN while he stays planted — the floor does NOT contest the tether (the predator won't blow its ambush over a chain at the door; the haven wants him to COME IN). Instead the ILLUSION DOUBLES DOWN as he hauls truth out (welcome warms, host more insistent, gold re-drapes the gap) — lying harder to lure, NOT a grab/threat-state change. ARMED BOUND: the grab/reel becomes a live fair consequence ONLY if HE crosses the plane (leans/commits his body past the threshold for reach, or anchors himself to the chain) — the line is the rule. LOOT (bounded): grim real climber bones (physical proof) + ONE modest tangible (pitted iron spike / broken blade, minor atk ~2-3 / cold-iron forge stock); kept small so threshold salvage doesn't pre-empt the deeper reward path; no second warning-note (the hall's corpse-note is the lore-gate); the near-pile is EXHAUSTIBLE (a few tries strips reachable substrate, then more wants a step in). Mechanics: weld = routine Smithing (modest ember/focus draw, core spent-low since t68); throw-and-catch = improvised 1d20 FINESSE, low DC vs the stationary near-pile, 'many tries' = success assured, rolls set speed/quality."},"id":"d6bcf9d9-b1ef-5954-96ea-c7aa85e75f78"}
