-        "detail": "engine/engine.ts is the resolution authority (surfaced as the action-resolution policy anchor). Each resolved action appends a roll-log entry carrying the full field set (turn / action / attr / die / roll / score / DC / margin / result) so any GM reproduces the outcome from the record rather than trusting a narrated result. Logging is a seed obligation; migrating the roll engine to a repo verb is out of scope.",
-        "requirement": "Every resolved action's roll is logged so the record is reproducible — the roll-log entry carries turn, action, attr, die, roll, score, DC, margin, and result. The engine is the resolution authority (see the action-resolution policy); never hand-write a derived outcome."
