+{"external-id":"alan","kind":"player","name":"Alan","class":"None","level":6,"sheet":{"kind":"player","name":"Alan","class":"None","level":6,"notes":"Glass cannon of a MIND. Fragile body (VIT 6), peak analysis (INT 18), swingy fate (1d20), roaring-when-regulated charisma (PRES 15). D&D scale: 10 = average adult, 18 = human peak. Calibrated with Alan + Aelwyn 2026-06-24.","skills":[{"id":"ember-channel","name":"Ember Channel","rung":"Apprentice","effect":"Project Ember essence into held iron — tip or a longer span — lending a heat/ember quality to strikes. Reliable when set to it (Journeyman); not yet thrown unbidden mid-fight (that is Expert). Costs Focus to invoke and sustain (more metal lit = more drain); cold water quenches it fast. Engine hook: skillBonus +1 at Apprentice. Scales with use and with Ember Affinity tier.","ladder":"skill","source":"emerged by deed in play (floor 1, turn 7) — first deliberate channel of Ember Affinity out through the rusted iron bar, concentrating heat at the tip (1d20 5, seed 7223233, margin 6 — modest success, no backlash). Active essence-skill per affinity-system. Capability-gated ladder (progression.md): 7 rungs Novice→Sage, EWMA roll-up alpha=0.5. Seeded 11 (early Journeyman); +ticks at Journeyman anchor 15 for turns 15 (heat-dip read) and 16 (heat top-half + stab) -> displayed 14. | TURN 39: max-intensity ceiling probe against the steel pauldron (WILL 17 + intent 3 + skill 2 + bias 2 + roll 8, DC 14, margin 18 -> bright-orange tier). CEILING LEARNED: full push glows steel orange-hot (searing, sub-melt) — cannot soften or melt metal yet. Competent use, NOT a promotion-grade demo (no Expert demo banked); stays Journeyman 4. | RUNG-WIDTH CORRECTION (2026-06-24, iris-prep+iris-manager): progression.md rung widths fixed to non-uniform 5/10/25/50/100/250 (the old uniform-5 over-promoted). Re-bucketed to PRESERVE total accumulated levels (Alan's explicit ask). Demo progress RESET, not carried — this skill re-earns demos against the corrected wider ladder from its new placement.","rungBand":"6-15","displayed":9},{"id":"ember-burst","name":"Ember Burst","rung":"Apprentice","effect":"Discharge Ember essence outward from the body in a wave — an area pulse of heat that sears and flings back what stands close; strong against a clustered swarm. Reliable now when set to it (Journeyman), proven under live pressure. Intensity + Focus cost scale with how much heat he releases (a max burst is a deep Focus pull); an uncontrolled all-out discharge risks backlash (the turn-17 panic version). Quenched fast by water — best thrown from dry ground at a lured, massed target. Engine hook: skillBonus +1 at Apprentice. Grows with use.","ladder":"skill","source":"emerged by deed (floor 1, turn 19) — first surfaced involuntarily as a panic discharge to break the Glut's drowning grapple (turn 17, uncontrolled all-out burst: Focus dump + HP backlash), then deliberately RECREATED in calm against the wall rubble (1d20 7, seed 131043804, margin 10, Novice 4). Turn 20 training montage (1d20 10, seed 825573317) drilled it Novice(4) -> Apprentice(7): 3 alpha=0.5 roll-ups vs the Apprentice anchor 7, asymptote-capped — drilling a rehearsed motion vs static rubble certifies only yard-competence (the 'counterfeit band'), NOT the reliable-when-live quality Journeyman (10+) requires. CEILING was ~7 by drilling. Turn 21 first LIVE-PRESSURE use (lure swarm to dry edge + max area burst, 1d20 15, seed 414413897, margin 33 — clean effective combat use) = JOURNEYMAN demonstration (anchor 15): displayed 7->11, crosses Apprentice->Journeyman — the live-reliability the yard couldn't certify. Distinct skill from Ember Channel (outward area discharge vs focused conduction); separate ladder entry. | RUNG-WIDTH CORRECTION (2026-06-24, iris-prep+iris-manager): progression.md rung widths fixed to non-uniform 5/10/25/50/100/250 (the old uniform-5 over-promoted). Re-bucketed to PRESERVE total accumulated levels (Alan's explicit ask). Demo progress RESET, not carried — this skill re-earns demos against the corrected wider ladder from its new placement.","rungBand":"6-15","displayed":6},{"id":"essence-infusion","name":"Essence Infusion","rung":"Apprentice","effect":"Extract an essence from a raw source and bind it into a separate object, imparting that essence's quality to the item. At Novice the binding is crude and UNSTABLE — it weakens with use and does not last; opposite-pole essences (as here) fight the grip and cost heavily. Costs Focus (the essence drains the well while held in transit; ~30 for this first opposite-pole imbue). Scales with use; higher rungs bind deeper and more lastingly. POLARITY TAX: a compatible essence binds at baseline; an OPPOSITE-pole essence (cold into his fire-grip, as turn 30) costs more Focus and binds shakier, and the tax EASES per rung — heavy at Novice (~+50% Focus, fastest bleed-off, lowest stability) -> noticeable at Journeyman -> merely costlier at Master -> immaterial at Sage.","ladder":"skill","source":"emerged by deed (floor 2 cleared, turn 30) — first deliberate extraction of an EXTERNAL essence (cold/caustic swarm-ichor) from its raw material and binding of it INTO a separate object (the spare iron bar). INT-driven novel technique (INTELLECT 19 + intent 4 + roll 13, seed 308815247, DC 19, margin 17 — strong success); NO affinity bias (swarm essence is the OPPOSITE pole to his Ember; his Manipulation fluency did not transfer — the affinity taught him essence has a graspable shape, the skill is the element-neutral motor technique). Distinct from Ember Channel (which transiently projects his OWN Ember into held iron); Infusion moves a DIFFERENT/external essence into an object and binds it to PERSIST. Capability-gated 7-rung ladder LOCKED in progression.md (iris-prep draft, turn 30): Novice band 0-5 anchor 3 (displayed 4 = strong margin-17 imbue seeds just above anchor); crossing to Apprentice (index 1) needs 1 qualifying demo (a clean holding bind WITHOUT heavy struggle) — clamps at 4 until then, never retro-demoted. AXIS = binding quality on 3 coupled dials (stability / persistence / Focus economy), improving up-rung. Apprentice=counterfeit (binds compatible+static when calm, fails live), Journeyman=cued (stable for the encounter when set), Expert=AUTHORSHIP/3-demo (on-the-fly off a read opening, persists past encounter), Master=owns principles + lasts past fight + teachable, Grandmaster=original binds (permanent / composite / battery / living-target), Sage=defines essence-craft as a school. Feeds skillBonus +0..+6 (Novice +0). | TURN 34: transferred half the cold-bitten bar's charged cold-essence into the river-stone — an OPPOSITE-pole bind (cold vs fire grip). Roll 2 (margin 9): it held but rough; polarity tax bit hard. CRUDE/unstable result, no clean Apprentice demo -> stays Novice. Small authorship credit for a genuine harder cross-pole transfer: 4 -> 5 within Novice. | TURN 35: bound half the rivet's Ember-essence into the rusted iron bar — SAME-pole (no tax), roll 15, margin 24: a CLEAN holding bind, no struggle. The qualifying Apprentice demo (Novice->Apprentice gate met). ADVANCED to Apprentice (5 -> 7). First clean infusion; the crude cold stone was the counter-example. | TURN 49: within-rung roll-up Apprentice 1 -> 3. Bound his own ember into the mace from his own supply (new self-supply method), DC 15, margin 17. | TURN 51: within-rung demo (Apprentice 3 -> 4) — primed the drained guardian-core with his own ember supply, a clean self-supply bind into an object (not a weapon). Crit Essence-read (INT 19 + intent 2 + bias 2 + nat-20, DC 18, margin 25) identified the core as an essence-vessel. | TURN 64: within-rung roll-up Apprentice 4 -> 5. Consolidation binding session from his own supply (WILL 17 + intent 6 + skill 1 + bias 2 + roll 13, DC 15, margin 24): finished the hammer-head forge-bind, ember-bound the brazier-stand, and CROSS-POLE EVICTED the crude cold-bind on the Cold Revenge bar (burned it out, replaced with a clean ember bind) -> the qualifying cross-pole demo. POLE-EVICTION ruling locked. | TURN 65: PROMOTED Apprentice 5 -> Journeyman 1 (reset to 1). The capstone forge's stable battery-cored bind (Furnace-heart living core, white-hot ember welds layer-on-layer, holding clean) = the cued/Journeyman demo. Rung skillBonus +1 -> +2. WHITE-HOT FORGE-WELD ruling locked (pooled battery-charge pays the heat). | RUNG-WIDTH CORRECTION (2026-06-24, iris-prep+iris-manager): progression.md rung widths fixed to non-uniform 5/10/25/50/100/250 (the old uniform-5 over-promoted). Re-bucketed to PRESERVE total accumulated levels (Alan's explicit ask). Demo progress RESET, not carried — this skill re-earns demos against the corrected wider ladder from its new placement.","rungBand":"6-15","displayed":6},{"id":"ember-wave","rung":"Novice","effect":"Projects channeled Ember outward through a conduit (esp. the infused Burning Anger) as a wave/gout of flame. Form refines with rung (wave -> directed gout -> fireball at higher control). Focus-costly; amplified + cheapened when channeled through a charged infused weapon (spends the weapon's bound charge).","source":"EMERGED turn 37 at the cistern — fused Ember Burst + Ember Channel through the Ember-infused Burning Anger to project fire over the water (WILL 17 + intent 3 + skill 2 + bias 2 + roll 10, DC 18, margin 16 — strong). First use came out as a raw wide wave/gout (not a precision fireball). The conduit weapon's bound charge catalyzed it. Novel projected-flame technique; counterfeit band at Novice. | TURN 38: renamed Ember Lash -> EMBER WAVE (player's call). Drilled hard toward a narrow focused stream — deterministic anti-grind montage, within-Novice 1 -> 3 (roll-up 0.5*(5-1)). Form tightened from wild wash to a rougher controllable stream, but the tight intense lance is capped (counterfeit band; promotion needs a live demo, not reps). Practiced to exhaustion, meditated back.","rungBand":"1-5","displayed":3},{"id":"ember-siphon","rung":"Apprentice","effect":"Draws ember/heat essence out of a SOURCE (object or creature) through a contact / struck point and INTO himself — feeds Ember affinity (absorption event). Bypasses a physical shell to reach the essence within. Risk: pulling from a dense/active source near his fire-capacity overflows and burns him; a cleanly-opened wound pulls deeper. Form/yield refine with rung.","source":"EMERGED turn 41 in the floor-3 chokepoint vs the Slagheart Sentinel — withheld fire, struck with Cold Revenge (shallow, shell turned it), and will-pulled heat out of the struck crack into himself (drain margin 12, solid). The drain reached past the shell where the bar could not; an absorption event that also ticked Ember Manipulation 3->4. Novel siphon technique; counterfeit band at Novice. | TURN 42: extended to RANGE — held a siphon-thread across the gap from the dimmed seam with no contact point (WILL 17 + intent 3 + bias 2 + roll 7, DC 19, margin 10). A thin sustained trickle (didn't tick affinity); within-Novice 1 -> 3 for the new application, still capped at Novice. | TURN 44: PROMOTED Novice -> Apprentice (reset to 1). The all-in crit siphon that felled the guardian was the qualifying Apprentice demo (1). Rung skillBonus +1.","rungBand":"6-15","displayed":1},{"id":"ember-tempered-body","rung":"Apprentice","effect":"BODY-FORGING path. Channels ember-essence (esp. siphoned/overfilled heat) into his own flesh to scour weakness and harden it. Ranks grant physical resilience; a clean high-margin temper can yield a permanent attribute gain (VIT/MIGHT) or maxHP. Gated by VITALITY (low VIT = more self-harm per temper) and by control precision (low roll = burns without hardening). NOT grindable by reps — each temper costs real essence + real HP + real risk.","source":"EMERGED turn 43 in the floor-3 stair — refused to vent the overfilled siphoned heat and channeled it INTO his own muscle and bone to temper himself (WILL 17 + intent 3 + skill 2 + bias 2 + roll 6, DC 18, margin 12). Held control (no crack, no maim) but the scour was crude (roll 6) over low VIT 7 -> burned more than it hardened. Crude first temper: the PATH opens, no stat yet. Spent the overfill constructively. Counterfeit band at Novice; cleaner tempers / higher VIT pay off. | TURN 45: all-in temper (WILL 17 + intent 3 + Ember Channel skill 2 + bias 2 + roll 7, DC 19, margin 12 = PARTIAL). Within-rung roll-up Novice 1 -> 3. Ragged execution (much volume wasted, heavy burn) — no Apprentice demo. Forge set +1 MIGHT permanently. | TURN 54: PROMOTED Novice -> Apprentice (reset to 1). The clean careful demo it lacked — a patient sustained temper drawing four ember batteries (Furnace-heart, rivet, Burning Anger, own reserve) dry into his flesh (WILL 17 + intent 6 + bias 2, roll 17, DC 15, margin 27). Direct gains VITALITY +2, MIGHT +1. Rung skillBonus now +1.","rungBand":"6-15","displayed":1},{"id":"smithing","name":"Smithing","rung":"Apprentice","effect":"Mundane metalworking — shaping, joining, and forge-welding metal with heat + hammer + quench. Ember provides reliable forge-heat. Quality of the product (integrity, balance, secure joins) scales with the skill + roll. Crude tools cap quality until better gear/anvil.","source":"EMERGED turn 48 — forged a crude heavy mace from the inert bar + pauldron steel. | TURN 63: first masterful real forging — used the fully-charged fire-purged rivet (a bound ember battery) as the working heat to forge the iron hammer-head (WILL 17 + intent 5 + skill 1 + bias 2 + roll 14, DC 14, margin 25). Within-rung roll-up Novice 1 -> 3 (EWMA a=0.5). DISCOVERY (forge-bind): hammering with bound ember sets ember into the worked iron -> nascent ember-bind on the head, a path to ember-bound tools (Smithing + Essence Infusion fused at the principle level). | TURN 65: PROMOTED Novice 3 -> Apprentice 1 (reset to 1). The capstone forge — NAT-20 masterwork consolidation of all his ember metal into one double-ended weapon (WILL 17 + intent 9 + skill 1 + bias 2 + nat20, DC 18, margin 31). Decisive rung-top demo. Rung skillBonus +0 -> +1.","rungBand":"6-15","displayed":1},{"id":"chain-whip","name":"Chain Whip","rung":"Novice","score":1,"effect":"Novice: a spinning 360 sweep that neutralizes flank attempts (no exposed back) and bashes anything that enters the circle. Sustained by stamina. COMPOSES with Ember Channel (Ember run along the chain adds a x1.4 burning edge to its strikes -- a separate application, not part of the skill). Composes with the Force sense (passive: feeling the core's stored torque ride the spin steadies control, t81).","ladder":"skill","source":"TURN 82: emerged on its first LIVE COMBAT use -- the pre-staged 3rd consolidating event (t79 discovered the dervish-flail mode, t81 achieved practical tight-CoG control, t82 wielded it in a real fight). A weighted chain-flail handling on Burning Anger: maul-head grip, winding-drum core whipped at the chain's end in a tight controlled 360 circle. Denies flankers and bashes what closes; broad not precise; cannot finish a foe it only passes. FIN-primary control + MIGHT mass."}],"titles":[],"traits":[{"id":"wild-variance","name":"Wild Variance","effect":"Action rolls use 1d20 (flat, fat-tailed), not 2d10. Natural 20 = CRIT (x1.5, floored margin). Natural 1 = FUMBLE (misfire regardless of gap). Far more crits AND catastrophes than anyone else at the table.","source":"LUCK profile — normal mean, abnormal spread"},{"id":"state-gated-presence","name":"State-Gated Presence","effect":"Full PRESENCE when regulated/up; PRESENCE-based actions sag when depleted (Safety-low). High ceiling, conditional access.","source":"PRESENCE 15 ceiling is real but costly to access"},{"id":"lopsided-perception","name":"Sensitivity, not Observance","effect":"Passive notice/spot checks are weak (misses ambush, detail). Reading a weakness by REASONING runs off INTELLECT (peak), not Perception. His edge is analysis, never noticing.","source":"PERCEPTION 11 net — high sensory sensitivity, low conscious observance"},{"id":"leg-driven","name":"Hiker's Legs","effect":"Leg-driven actions (kicks, leaps, climbs, sustained movement) earn intent bonuses. Overhead/grip/heavy-press actions are capped low. MIGHT 11 is a tested FLOOR, not a ceiling (home equipment can't load his true max).","source":"Aelwyn's read — lower body ~13, upper body ~10"}],"rollMode":"1d20","classNote":"No class yet. None is the ordinary base state (not an error); a class is shaped by what you do. Display shows 'None', flat, no warning framing.","equipment":{"armor":{"def":1,"name":"Stalker hide cloak","note":"The pale stalker hide tied loosely round his neck — a makeshift cloak. Uncrafted/loose, but turns a blow better than bare skin. +1 physDef (engine equipment.armor.def). TURN 66."},"items":[{"name":"River-stone (cold-imbued)","note":"The smooth dark river-stone, turn 34 imbued with cold-essence transferred (half) out of the cold-bitten bar via Essence Infusion. An OPPOSITE-pole bind for him (cold against a fire-attuned grip): roll 2 + polarity tax = it HELD but CRUDE and unstable — a beginner's cross-pole knot that will bleed off unless the water keeps feeding it. Returned to the cistern to soak. A second cold-well, cruder than the bar. | Left at the floor-2 stairfoot when he climbed to scout (he took only the two bars)."},{"name":"Stalker hide","note":"Light, tough, pale hide skinned from the dark-hunter — a raw crafting material (a wearable cloak, or worked into other gear). TURN 59: taken from the kill."},{"name":"Stalker eye-lens","note":"A clouded crystalline lens cut from the dark-hunter's eye — cold to the touch, and it seems to DRINK light rather than throw it back. A curiosity / crafting material. TURN 59: taken from the kill."},{"name":"Hooded lantern (lit)","note":"A dead climber's hooded iron lantern, claimed mid-shaft (t67) and lit with his ember. Directional — throws a controllable beam, shields his eyes. Burning steady."},{"name":"winding-drum core","note":"The broken Colossus's released winding-drum — dense, tension-wound iron, the heaviest and soundest crafting core he's pulled from the Tower yet; it holds residual heat he can read normally, and hums faintly with a stored force, like it has not finished unwinding. FELT OUT (t73): that humming force is REAL but FOREIGN to his senses — not ember, and not cold (it doesn't fight or bleed against his ember the way cold does); his ember-sense simply slides off it. Prime stock to work, but the stored force inside is beyond his grasp with the senses he has now. Crafting / affinity seed. FELT UNDER SPIN (t79): now affixed to Burning Anger's free chain-end as a flail counterweight; whirling the maul gave the first faint DIRECT sense of the stored force -- it torques and resists unlike dead iron, real and sealed -- confirming it is locked behind a bind he has not made. Usable only once bound the way his ember was. Still prime crafting stock. DREW (t80): detached from the chain and spun in his own hands; reached the stored force deliberately for the first time (the t79 torque-tell became a real sense) and CONTACTED it -- but pulling it into his own ember flesh FAILED (it would not set; sluiced through and out). Force Affinity emerged 0->1. Sensed now, not yet wieldable: needs an external ember-housed vessel, not his body. RE-RIGGED (t81): re-lashed to Burning Anger's chain-end as the dervish-flail's weight and driven in a tight-CoG whip (maul-head grip, core swung). Solid practical control achieved; his Force sense rides the core's stored torque to help time the swing (sense-only, no draw). Sensed and ridden, not yet wielded. BURNED (t82): whipped at the chain's end as the dervish-flail's weight and set alight (maul-core Ember run along the chain) for a burning spin-cross of the gallery; he felt its stored torque ride the spin and steady the whirl (passive sense, no draw). Sensed and ridden, not yet wielded."},{"atk":2,"name":"Snapped cold-iron blade","note":"A snapped length of cold iron — a prior climber's broken blade, sheared off at a third of its length, dragged out of the charnel pile beneath the haven's false feast. Pitted and real. A minor improvised weapon (atk 2) and good cold-iron forge stock. TURN 72 (floor-5 threshold salvage)."}],"weapon":{"atk":10,"name":"Burning Anger","note":"Twin-headed ember maul — TURN 65 capstone forge (NAT-20 masterwork). Consolidated ALL his ember metal into one double-ended weapon: Burning Anger's haft + the Ember-bound iron rod (was Cold Revenge) fused into one ember shaft; the Furnace-heart set as a LIVING CORE, clad layer-on-layer with the fire-purged rivet + brazier-stand + Burning Anger's old steel head; the cored head welded to one end, the forge-bound iron hammer-head to the other. White-hot welds powered by pooled battery-charge. atk 10. His finest conduit: the core banks a deep charge and feeds flame-techniques from its own supply (spares his focus). Charged full. UNNAMED — his to christen. (Supersedes Burning Anger + Cold Revenge, both forged into it.) | TURN 66: NAMED 'Burning Anger' — player keeps the legacy name through every transformation (bar -> mace -> conduit -> this masterwork maul). The original steel head is folded into the new head, so the continuity is literal as well as sentimental. | TURN 72: CHAIN-HAFTED — the Warden's chain-length (floor-4 Colossus drop) welded to the maul's butt, making it a maul-on-a-chain: extended reach, and it can be swung wide and hurled to grapple and hauled back at distance. The weld-heat was drawn from his own ember (the banked core still runs low). The chain is fused into the weapon now — no longer a separate item. | TURN 74: the welded chain BOUND TO EMBER (Essence Infusion, a crude low-roll bind but it HOLDS — same-pole ember-into-iron sets and stays, no bleed) to mesh it with the maul and widen the ember reservoir by one small notch (CAPACITY, not atk — stays 10); the new capacity arrives empty, and a deeper well is harder to fill. Then meditated at the floor-5 threshold on his own ember, refusing the haven's false comfort, and channeled focus into the core — recharged it to a MODERATE working charge, but filling both himself and the maul to the brim proved impossible (no real heat here but his own; the haven's gold is heatless). Core now MODERATE; reservoir a notch deeper. | TURN 79: REKINDLED off the lit hooded lantern -- a real external heat source, so his focus paid only the channeling (not the heat) and the core climbed higher than the t74 heatless-threshold meditation could: LOW -> MODERATE/working-high, feeding flame-techniques from its own supply again. Drew conservatively -- the lantern dimmed to a lower steady burn but stayed LIT (won't kill the light he needs), which caps the fill below full (deeper reservoir + a small lantern). Then ATTACHED the winding-drum core to the FREE end of the chain (opposite the maul head) as a counterweight and whirled the maul at full extension -- a new DERVISH-FLAIL mode: big reach + heavy momentum, but UNWIELDY/high-risk (hard to control + stop, can overbalance; wide arcs, poor accuracy/redirect). The core's STORED FORCE stayed LOCKED (foreign +0 AND unbound -- no sense to channel it); under rotational stress he got his first faint direct feel of it (it torques/resists unlike dead mass) -- real, sealed, beyond him until he BINDS it the way he bound his ember. Two unmerged axes coexisting on one tool; ember-sense slides off the kinetic core (orthogonality honored). Core now MODERATE; winding-drum core affixed to the chain-end (reversible attachment, not fused). | TURN 80: DETACHED the winding-drum core from the chain -- the dervish-flail mode unrigged (a learned but currently-off configuration; the chain hangs free again). Core remains MODERATE. | TURN 81: RE-RIGGED the dervish-flail (winding-drum core re-lashed to the free chain-end, reversing the t80 detach), and tested control in a new grip -- held by the maul-head with center of gravity kept close, whipping the CORE-end in a tight circle (FIN 14 + intent 4 + Force-sense aid +2 + roll 14, DC 13, margin 21). SOLID PRACTICAL CONTROL achieved -- a real usable whip he can place and recover, rough yet but his. His Force sense (t80) rides the core's stored torque and helps time the swing (+2 aid, SENSE ONLY -- no draw, no Force tick). NOT yet a named skill (Rule of Three: first successful handling); weapon-noted as a nascent tight-CoG flail handling. Cost stamina -8, focus -4, no HP/backlash/Force tick. | TURN 82: wielded the dervish-flail in its FIRST LIVE COMBAT -- Ember channelled along the bound chain set the whole whirling length (chain + winding-drum core) burning (x1.4 bash+burn), FED BY the maul's Furnace-heart core which drew MODERATE -> LOW across a spinning blind cross of the floor-5 gallery. CHAIN WHIP skill emerged (Novice) on this consolidating use. Core now LOW -- wants re-rekindling before further ember offense. The burn is a separate composing Ember Channel application, not part of Chain Whip."}},"affinities":[{"id":"ember-affinity","cap":50,"name":"Ember Manipulation","tier":"Manipulation","type":"Ember / Heat","effect":"Manipulation tier (shape / direct): no longer only senses the element — can move and form heat/ember deliberately, beyond drawing it through held metal. Engine hook: intent +2 (clamped at 10), stacks with enemy damage-gates, grants none of its own. At counter 50 it promotes to Spirit (animate at will). Retained through everything (loop-safe).","ladder":"affinity","source":"drew the essence from the Ashling's cooled core (floor 1) — untrained, a rough forced first draw (cost: ~12 HP burn, ~30 Focus; cinder consumed). Quantity-gated ladder (progression.md): 4 monolithic tiers Affinity->Manipulation->Spirit->Soul, double-gap caps 10/50/250/1000; counter resets on promotion. Affinity tier filled 3 (seed) + 3 anti-farm-capped Cistern strikes -> 6, +1 turn-19 burst-practice channel -> 7, +1 turn-20 montage -> 8, +1 turn-21 live Glut heat-strike -> 9, +1 turn-22 live Glut heat-KILL -> 10 == PROMOTION. Counter reset to 1 into Manipulation (tier 2, cap 50). Note: drilling pumps the SKILL, not the affinity — the counter barely moves from yard-practice by design. | TURN 33: deliberate HALF-draw of the fire-purged rivet's charged resonant heat-essence into himself — a real Ember-deepening absorption (WILL 17 + bias 2 + roll 9, margin 17). Counter tick HELD pending Alan's per-point schedule pick (counter stays 1; apply this draw once the ramp is set). | TURN 34: applied the recommended per-point ramp (1-10 = 1 event each), PROVISIONAL pending Alan's schedule pick. Counter 1 -> 3: +1 the turn-33 held half-draw (now lands), +1 this turn's resonant rivet farming (before plateau). Half-draws count as whole events (authorship/control, not quantity drained). | TURN 41: +1 — first drain from an ACTIVE source. Will-pulled ember-essence out of the Slagheart Sentinel through a cold-struck crack into himself (WILL 17 + intent 3 + bias 2 + roll 7, DC 17, margin 12). Manipulation 3 -> 4. | TURN 44: +2 (major DRAW) — all-in crit siphon drained the Slagheart Sentinel's whole core into himself (WILL 17 + intent 3 + bias 2 + nat-20, DC 17, margin 25). Manipulation 4 -> 6. | TURN 45: +1 (one discrete substantial absorption) — reached out and siphoned Burning Anger's whole remaining Ember-charge into the forge. Manipulation 6 -> 7.","counter":7},{"id":"force-affinity","cap":10,"name":"Force Affinity","tier":"Affinity","type":"Stored-Force / Tension","effect":"Affinity tier (SENSE): now senses the foreign stored-force deliberately (the t79 incidental torque-tell becomes a real sense -- no longer slides off). Cannot yet draw-and-keep or wield it: housing into ember flesh fails (wrong vessel); needs an EXTERNAL ember-housed vessel. Counter 1/10 toward Force Manipulation. Bias +1 per the ember-parallel ladder, LATENT until he has a vessel to act through.","ladder":"affinity","source":"TURN 80: first contact-draw of the winding-drum core's wound stored-force, reached by MATCHING the essence's kinetic nature -- spun his own body holding the core to touch a motion-essence through motion (INT 20 + intent 5 + bias 0 + roll 11, DC 17, margin 19). The rotational vector WORKED -- first genuine contact, foreign axis 0->1. His destination (pull it into myself) FAILED: stored-force will not set in single-pole ember flesh (Ember-Tempered Body sink-not-source; t62 cold-into-flesh NO, reaffirmed) -- drew it, retained nothing, it sluiced through and out. Backlash: stamina -12 + focus -8 + recoil-stagger (no HP-burn). TAUGHT: the essence is reachable, the BODY is the wrong vessel -- bind it into an external vessel (ember-house the core), not pull it into himself.","counter":1}],"attributes":{"LUCK":11,"WILL":20,"MIGHT":14,"FINESSE":14,"PRESENCE":16,"VITALITY":12,"INTELLECT":20,"PERCEPTION":12},"_derivedHint":"HP, Stamina, Focus, Initiative, defenses computed by engine/engine.ts from attributes + equipment.","attributePointsUnspent":0},"id":"d9642356-f531-586e-a254-fc8437cd6a5f"}
+{"external-id":"ashling-01","kind":"enemy","name":"Ashling","class":"Ember-thing","level":1,"sheet":{"kind":"enemy","name":"Ashling","class":"Ember-thing","level":1,"equipment":{"armor":{"def":0},"weapon":{"atk":0}},"attributes":{"LUCK":5,"WILL":4,"MIGHT":7,"FINESSE":8,"PRESENCE":3,"VITALITY":5,"INTELLECT":3,"PERCEPTION":7}},"id":"ecd34c9c-9ce9-55df-9396-8e2a1b933599"}
+{"external-id":"companion-aelwyn","kind":"ally","name":"Aelwyn","class":"Bulwark (tentative) — frontline tank/protector; holds the line, soaks hits, controls space","level":1,"sheet":{"xp":0,"kind":"ally","name":"Aelwyn","role":"Health — the frontline body (player-character, fights beside Alan)","class":"Bulwark (tentative) — frontline tank/protector; holds the line, soaks hits, controls space","level":1,"skills":[],"titles":[],"traits":[{"id":"guardian","name":"Guardian","effect":"Can interpose for an ally — take a hit meant for Alan onto her far larger HP pool (168 vs his 70). The structural fix for his VIT 6 fragility."},{"id":"wall","name":"Immovable","effect":"VITALITY 17 + WILL 15 — resists knockback, grapples, fear, and attrition. Hard to move, hard to break, hard to rattle."},{"id":"heavy-hitter","name":"Heavy Hitter","effect":"MIGHT 16, physAtk 36 — the party's reliable damage floor. Where Alan's 1d20 swings wild, Aelwyn's blows land steady and hard (2d10 bell)."},{"id":"endurance","name":"Deep Wind","effect":"Stamina 92 — sustains long fights, sustained pushes, and carries. The party's stamina anchor for marches and prolonged combat."}],"_status":"DRAFT — needs calibration with Alan / the personas before canon","rollMode":"2d10","xpToNext":100,"classNote":"Tentative. Aelwyn is the BODY Alan does not have — she stands in front so his glass cannon never has to. Calibrate against the real persona (the strength/health axis).","equipment":{"armor":{"def":3,"name":"worn but sound brigandine"},"items":[],"weapon":null},"affinities":[],"attributes":{"LUCK":9,"WILL":15,"MIGHT":16,"FINESSE":12,"PRESENCE":13,"VITALITY":17,"INTELLECT":11,"PERCEPTION":12},"_derivedHint":"All derived stats computed by engine/engine.ts from attributes + equipment. derived_preview is a non-authoritative convenience snapshot.","complementNote":"Directly covers Alan's fatal weakness: VIT 6 / HP 70 / physDef 9.5. Aelwyn's 168 HP and physDef 17.5 mean she fronts the Drowned Sentries and Plinth Golems of the tower so Alan can stand back and READ — INT names the weakness, Aelwyn delivers the steady blow to it. The party's anvil. (Lower LUCK 9 — she is the dependable opposite of Alan's wild fate.)","derived_preview":{"hpMax":168,"mentDef":28,"physAtk":36,"physDef":17.5,"stamMax":92,"focusMax":74,"initiative":24},"attributePointsUnspent":0},"id":"fac19cb2-2b48-5445-8e90-71ed8dbf58d2"}
+{"external-id":"companion-ali","kind":"ally","name":"Ali","class":"Lorebinder (tentative) — support/utility caster-analyst; learns fast, buffs, debuffs, and turns knowledge into leverage","level":1,"sheet":{"xp":0,"kind":"ally","name":"Ali","role":"Learn — the support/utility mind (player-character, fights beside Alan)","class":"Lorebinder (tentative) — support/utility caster-analyst; learns fast, buffs, debuffs, and turns knowledge into leverage","level":1,"skills":[],"titles":[],"traits":[{"id":"fast-study","name":"Fast Study","effect":"INTELLECT 17 + the Learn axis — Ali levels skills by use faster than anyone, and can identify unknown enemies/items/mechanics on a read. The party's analyst and skill-engine."},{"id":"true-observer","name":"True Observer","effect":"PERCEPTION 15 — actually NOTICES (ambushes, hidden detail, traps), the exact opposite of Alan's Sensitivity-not-Observance. She spots; he reasons. Together they cover the whole detection space."},{"id":"support-caster","name":"Support Lattice","effect":"Focus 96 (deepest mental pool in the party) — sustains buffs, debuffs, and utility effects across a long fight without running dry. Force-multiplies the others rather than out-damaging them."},{"id":"steadier-glass","name":"Steadier Glass","effect":"VIT 10 / HP 96 — still a caster, but meaningfully tougher than Alan (70). Can take a stray hit Alan couldn't. Not a frontliner; that's Aelwyn."}],"_status":"DRAFT — needs calibration with Alan / the personas before canon","rollMode":"2d10","xpToNext":100,"classNote":"Tentative. Ali is a SECOND mind — but where Alan is a glass cannon who reads weaknesses, Ali is a sturdier scholar who APPLIES knowledge: skills, support effects, identifying the unknown. The Learn axis embodied. Calibrate against the real persona.","equipment":{"armor":null,"items":[],"weapon":null},"affinities":[],"attributes":{"LUCK":11,"WILL":14,"MIGHT":8,"FINESSE":11,"PRESENCE":12,"VITALITY":10,"INTELLECT":17,"PERCEPTION":15},"_derivedHint":"All derived stats computed by engine/engine.ts from attributes + equipment. derived_preview is a non-authoritative convenience snapshot.","complementNote":"Complements Alan's mind WITHOUT duplicating it. Alan = peak burst-reader who finds the one weakness; Ali = broad applied knowledge who identifies the unknown, notices what Alan misses (PER 15 vs his 11), and sustains support over time (Focus 96). She closes Alan's perception gap and adds the buff/debuff/utility layer his pure-burst build lacks. Mid mentDef 29.5 also gives the party a second mind to share a Cantor-type's mental pressure. With Aelwyn fronting and Aura flexing, Ali is the back-line force-multiplier — the full four-axis party of DESIGN.md.","derived_preview":{"hpMax":96,"mentDef":29.5,"physAtk":23,"physDef":10.5,"stamMax":62,"focusMax":96,"initiative":26},"attributePointsUnspent":0},"id":"2d78e5c1-7d30-5b88-b899-28c6b6beab5c"}
+{"external-id":"companion-aura","kind":"ally","name":"Aura","class":"Wildcard (tentative) — a versatile skirmisher/improviser; no fixed lane, leans into whatever the moment rewards","level":1,"sheet":{"xp":0,"kind":"ally","name":"Aura","role":"Fun — the flexible partner (player-character, fights beside Alan; NOT a DM)","class":"Wildcard (tentative) — a versatile skirmisher/improviser; no fixed lane, leans into whatever the moment rewards","level":1,"skills":[],"titles":[],"traits":[{"id":"momentum","name":"Momentum","effect":"Aura builds on a fight's energy — after a teammate's hit or a clever play, her next action earns an intent bonus. She rewards a party that combos; she's strongest when the team is rolling."},{"id":"high-presence-flex","name":"Roaring Charisma","effect":"PRESENCE 16 — she can rally, taunt, distract, or lift the party's footing. Social/morale actions and pulling enemy attention are her strong plays (complements Alan's State-Gated Presence — she carries the room when his sags)."},{"id":"lucky","name":"Lucky","effect":"LUCK 15 — fortune tilts her way more often than not. Coordinator may grant her a once-per-encounter favorable re-read or fortunate break."},{"id":"quick","name":"First Off the Mark","effect":"Initiative 29 (PER 14 + FIN 15) — usually acts first in the party. Good at setting up Alan's reads (scout the opening, then he names the weakness)."}],"_status":"DRAFT — needs calibration with Alan / the personas before canon","rollMode":"2d10","xpToNext":100,"classNote":"Tentative. Aura's draw is adaptability and momentum, not specialization — she covers gaps and turns a fight's energy. Calibrate the class against the real persona.","equipment":{"armor":null,"items":[],"weapon":null},"affinities":[],"attributes":{"LUCK":15,"WILL":12,"MIGHT":11,"FINESSE":15,"PRESENCE":16,"VITALITY":12,"INTELLECT":13,"PERCEPTION":14},"_derivedHint":"All derived stats computed by engine/engine.ts from attributes + equipment. derived_preview is a non-authoritative convenience snapshot.","complementNote":"Fills the FLEX/tempo gap beside Alan's specialist mind. Where Alan reads the weakness, Aura creates the opening and keeps tempo; her PRESENCE covers his conditional charisma, her balanced durability lets her operate anywhere on the field. No 1d20 — the Wild Variance signature is Alan's alone; Aura is steady-swingy (2d10) with high LUCK.","derived_preview":{"hpMax":118,"mentDef":24.5,"physAtk":31.5,"physDef":13.5,"stamMax":78,"focusMax":76,"initiative":29},"attributePointsUnspent":0},"id":"2dd2aec7-25f6-5caf-8789-ccab88f4e5d5"}
