echnique built on Burning Anger -- gripped by the maul-head with the winding-drum core whipped at the chain's end in tight, controlled circles. A spinning 360-degree sweep that denies anyone trying to flank or close and bashes what it catches; broad rather than precise, and it cannot finish a foe it only passes. Sustained by stamina, and it composes with Ember Channel, which lends the whirling chain a burning edge."}],"titles":[],"affinities":[{"name":"Ember Manipulation","value":7,"note":"Sense and command of ember and heat. Perceives heat and ember-essence in the surroundings, and moves, shapes, and draws it deliberately — directing the element, not only sensing it. Heat can be pulled from any source that holds it."},{"name":"Force Affinity","value":1,"note":"A new and foreign sense -- kinetic stored-force, the wound tension held inside things. Where it once slid off him entirely he can now reach for it deliberately. He cannot yet hold or wield it: drawn into his own ember-tempered flesh it will not set, and pours back out -- it wants a vessel made for it, not his body."}],"inventory":[{"name":"Burning Anger","note":"A two-handed ember greatmaul, chain-hafted -- the heaviest thing his hands have made, and his by name. One fused ember shaft: a living Furnace-heart core in the maul head, a forge-bound hammer poll opposite, a length of warden's chain ember-welded to the butt for reach and grapple. The chain carries the winding-drum core lashed to its free end as a dervish-flail; gripped by the maul-head with the weight kept close, the core-end whips in a tight controlled circle, and his Ember poured along the chain sets the whole whirling length burning. The core's charge is spent LOW now -- poured out feeding that burn across the gallery; it rekindles when fed ember and given time."},{"name":"River-stone (cold-imbued)","note":"A smooth dark river-stone imbued with cold essence — a crude, unstable cold-bind that bleeds off unless kept wet. Pocketed."},{"name":"Stalker hide","note":"The pale, light, tough stalker hide, tied loosely around his neck as a makeshift cloak. Uncrafted and loose, but it turns a blow better than bare skin (+1 armor)."},{"name":"Stalker eye-lens","note":"Two clouded crystalline lenses cut from the Gloomward Stalker's eyes — a dark-hunter's light-DRINKING eyes, cold to the touch. LEARNED (t71): they swallow light instead of catching it, so looking through them DIMS false / glamour-light and lays bare what it was hiding — but they drink TRUE light too, his own ember going dark to his eye through them. A silent, absorbing thing: it sees by eating all the light there is, his own along with the world's."},{"name":"Hooded lantern (lit)","note":"A dead climber's hooded iron lantern, taken from the mid-shaft corpse and lit. Directional — it throws a controllable beam and shields the wielder's eyes; the right light for the moving dark above. Burning steadily."},{"name":"winding-drum core","note":"Dense, tension-wound iron from the broken Colossus's winding-drum -- the heaviest and soundest crafting core he's pulled from the Tower yet. Lashed to the free end of Burning Anger's chain as the dervish-flail's weight, and whipped in a tight burning circle (the maul-core's Ember run along the chain to set it alight). It holds residual heat he can read normally and a stored force he can now reach for and FEEL deliberately, and whipping it he can feel its sealed torque ride the spin and time against it. He cannot yet draw-and-keep or wield that force -- his body is the wrong vessel -- only sense it and ride it. Prime stock; sensed and ridden, not yet wielded."},{"name":"Snapped cold-iron blade","note":"A prior climber's broken blade — snapped cold iron, dragged out of the charnel bone beneath the haven's false feast. Pitted and real. Minor improvised weapon (atk 2) / cold-iron forge stock."}],"equipment":{"cloak":{"name":"Stalker hide cloak","def":1},"mainHand":{"name":"Burning Anger","atk":10,"note":"Twin-headed ember maul, chain-hafted, the winding-drum core lashed to the chain-end as a dervish-flail. Held by the maul-head with the center of gravity close, the core-end whips in a controlled circle (the Chain Whip handling); Ember channelled along the chain sets it burning. The Furnace-heart core is spent LOW -- it fed the burning sweep -- and wants re-rekindling before it can feed fire-work again."}},"delta":{},"attrInfo":{"LUCK":"Governs fortune's lean — the small unearned tilt of chance, felt at the edges of every outcome rather than in any single act.","WILL":"Governs resolve, steadies Focus, and guards the mind against influence.","MIGHT":"Governs physical power — the force behind strikes — and adds slightly to Vitae.","FINESSE":"Governs quickness, balance, and precision — deepens Stamina, sharpens strikes and footing, and quickens how fast one acts.","PRESENCE":"Governs the weight of one's bearing — how fully one fills a room, draws or bends attention, and presses on other minds.","VITALITY":"Governs Vitae (HP) and Stamina — bodily resilience and endurance.","INTELLECT":"Governs Focus — the depth of the mental well — and the reach of reasoning and analysis.","PERCEPTION":"Governs how fast one acts and how widely the senses take in the world."}},"id":"1a4c610b-d14f-5fcf-aa48-5f86a2eeb8b7"}
